"hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:"
8017,"(8017) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, he said: Al-Safar bin Nasir Al-Asadi narrated to me, on the authority of Yazid bin Sharih Al-Hadrami, that he heard Abu Imamah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: None of you should perform the prayer. And it is an injection that will even reduce it. (Ahmad 5/250, Tabarani 7507)"
8018,"(8018) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Idris, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: None of you should stand up for prayer with any harm in him. (Ahmad 2/442, Ibn Hibban 2072)"
8019,"(8019) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Yahya ibn Ja’di, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: He does not approach the prayer with zina’. It was said: O Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and what is zina’? He said: The one who finds rice in his stomach."
8020,"(8020) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sadaqi, on the authority of Yahya bin Atiq, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: It is disliked to withhold harm unless one fears missing the prayer."
8021,"(8021) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Arqam, who said: He went out for Umrah with His companions gave the call to prayer and established the iqaamah, and said to some of his companions: Come forward. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: If you come Prayer and one of you wants to be alone, so start by being alone. (Tirmidh 142. Abu Dawud 89)"
8022,"(8022) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Nafi’ was asked about a man who finds bloating in his stomach? He said: He does not pray while he finds the blow."
8023,"(8023) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Hazra, a sheikh from the people of Medina, and he praised him well, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad said: Some of Aisha’s nephews entered her, so he went to the mosque, and she said to him: Sit, for I heard the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: None of you should pray by preparing food, nor should he defend the unclean. (Muslim 393. Ibn Hibban 2073)"
8024,"(8024) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Because I love to wrap it in my turban, then I stand up for prayer. I have to push him away while I pray, meaning defecation and urine."
8025,"(8025) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Bakr, who said: Because I shed water, perform tayammum, and pray, are more beloved to me than I pray while I defecate or urinate."
8026,"(8026) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who urinates or blows his nose, he said: He will pray as long as he does not hasten his prayer."
8027,"(8027) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I was informed on the authority of Tawus, who said: We will certainly help him with determination."
8028,"(8028) Hushaym and Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They mentioned the man who found himself urinating. Hushaym said: And he finds the blowing, should he perform ablution? He said: Then, by God, we will continue performing ablution."
8029,"(8029) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I mentioned that to Muhammad, and he said: They had seen him as never before."
8030,"(8030) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I told him: I find some urine to squeeze out, so you come to the prayer, so I pray. And I found it. He said: Yes, if you think that you will imprison him until you pray."
8031,"(8031) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, Amir and Ata’, they said: There is no harm in a man being given an injection."
8032,"(8032) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in a man injecting urine. He did not hasten him from bowing and prostrating."
8033,"(8033) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar said: I am calculating the portion of the two seas while I In prayer"
8034,"(8034) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, who said: Omar said: I am preparing my armies while I am in prayer."
8035,"(8035) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Muhammad about an imam who leads the people in prayer, standing in a corner. And there is no middle ground? He said: I don't know of any harm in it."
8036,"(8036) Bishr ibn Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Qurayh, he said: Abu Al-Ala’ used to show off in the shade with us and lead us in prayer in prayer. The mosque was."
8037,"(8037) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mugheerah bin Ziyad al-Mawsili narrated to us, saying: I saw Ata’ praying in the shed in The Sacred Mosque was in the crowd, and they were separated from the rows. I said to him, or it was said to him, and he said: He is an old and distinguished sheikh. Dawiya, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey and rain fell on him, so he led the people in prayer while they were on their journey. By Bilal, people heard the takbir."
8038,"(8038) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Kharit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Uqaili’s brother said: Ibn Abbas may have been safe in the corner of the mosque, but not in the middle."
8039,"(8039) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Arouba, he said: I saw Al-Hasan Al-Basri. He leads them in a corner."
8040,"(8040) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: Bilal said: O Messenger of God, do not precede me in trust. (Abu Dawud 934. Ahmad 6/15)"
8041,"(8041) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who narrated it, saying: If the reciter believes So they believed, and whoever matches his belief with the belief of the angels, his previous sins will be forgiven. (Bukhari 6402 and Muslim 72)"
8042,"(8042) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father, he said: I prayed He succeeded the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he said {not those with anger upon them nor those who have gone astray} he said: Amen. (Abdul Razzaq 2433. Ahmad 4/318)"
8043,"(8043) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Hijr bin Anbas, on the authority of Wael bin Hijr, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting: {And not those who go astray} and he said: Amen, extending his voice to it. (Tirmidhi 249. Abu Dawud 930)"
8044,"(8044) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra: that Gabriel, peace be upon him, recited The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, opened the Book, and when he said: {And not those who go astray} he said: Say Amen, so he said: Amen."
8045,"(8045) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Kathir ibn Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of al-Walid ibn Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: He was a muezzin in Bahrain, so he said to the imam: Do not outpace me, Amen."
8046,"(8046) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Fitr narrated to us, saying: I heard Ikrimah saying: I have met the people and they have hope in Their mosques are safe when the imam says: {Not those with anger upon them, nor those who go astray}"
8047,"(8047) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The imam was only appointed to be followed, so when he said: {other than the angry upon them, nor those who go astray. So say: Amen. (Ibn Majah 8461 Malik 45)"
8048,"(8048) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar example. (Muslim 63 Abu Dawud 964)"
8049,"(8049) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ali, who said: Al-Rabi’ ibn Khathim was The Imam said: {Not those with anger upon them, nor those who go astray} and he said: O God, forgive me, Amen."
8050,"(8050) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Bakr bin Ma’iz, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym, He said: If the imam says: {Not those with anger upon them, nor those who go astray}, then seek help from supplication with whatever you wish."
8051,"(8051) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was desirable if the imam said: {other than angered} On them and not those who go astray} to say: O God, forgive me, Amen."
8052,"(8052) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I prayed behind Abu Abdullah Al-Jadali, and when he said: {Ghayr Those with whom He is angry, nor those who go astray. He said: Allah is sufficient as a Guide and Helper."
8053,"(8053) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: If the imam says: {other than the angry Upon them, nor those who go astray} So say: O God, I ask you for Paradise and I seek refuge in You from Hell."
8054,"(8054) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, who said: Amen is one of the names of God."
8055,"(8055) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, similar to him."
8056,"(8056) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir, who said: Amen is one of the names of God."
8057,"(8057) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Amin is one of the names of God."
8058,"(8058) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: We had a loud noise in this mosque of ours, Amen. If the imam says: {Not those with anger upon them, nor those who go astray}"
8059,"(8059) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Mu’adh: that when he sealed the cows He said: Amen."
8060,"(8060) Omar bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Abu Hamza, the client of Al-Muhallab: that he prayed beside Saeed bin Jubair, when he said: {Not those with anger upon them, nor those who go astray} he said: Amen, or something with this meaning."
8061,"(8061) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad: That Abu Hurairah was a muezzin in Bahrain, so he said to the imam: No. You precede me, Amen."
8062,"(8062) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man, that whenever Mu’adh recited the last verse of Al-Baqarah {Then help us against the disbelieving people} He said: Amen."
8063,"(8063) Ibn Uyaynah told us, he said: Perhaps on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Al-Zubayr, he said: It was for the mosque. Hope, or he said deep, if the imam says: {Not those with anger upon them, nor those who go astray}"
8064,"(8064) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Ibn Sa’id Abi Al-Khudri, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you yawns during prayer, let him suppress it as much as he can, for Satan enters. (Muslim 58. Abu Dawud 4987)"
8065,"(8065) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Fazara al-Absi, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Asam, who said: He did not yawn. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the prayer of Qat."
8066,"(8066) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: If one of you yawns during prayer, let him place his hand on it."
8067,"(8067) On the authority of Qatada, similar to the hadith of Sufyan."
8068,"(8068) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali, who said: Yawning during prayer is from Satan. Sneezing and drowsiness are severe when preaching."
8069,"(8069) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: Yawning during prayer And sneezing is from Satan, so seek refuge in God from him."
8070,"(8070) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Indeed, I ward off yawning during prayer by sighing."
8071,"(8071) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he yawned during prayer, he His lips and wiped his nose."
8072,"(8072) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, who said: I was informed that Satan has a bottle that people smell during prayer so that they may yawn."
8073,"(8073) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: A man stops yawning during prayer. As long as he is able, if he is defeated, he puts his hand on his mouth."
8074,"(8074) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: Yawning during prayer is from Satan."
8075,"(8075) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd. He said: Satan has A flask in which blows are blown, so when they stand up for prayer, they blow it open, and at that they are ordered to scatter it."
8076,"(8076) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Ma’shar told us, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: God He hates yawning and loves sneezing during prayer."
8077,"(8077) Waki` told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: If he yawns during prayer Let him refrain from reciting Qur’an."
8078,"(8078) Abu Khaled told us, not by Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: If one of you yawns while he is reciting, let him refrain from reciting."
8079,"(8079) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of his uncle: He complained to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. A man finds something in prayer and he clings to it. He said: Nothing is obligatory for him until he finds it. His scent, and he hears its voice. (Bukhari 1371, Abu Dawud 178)"
8080,"(8080) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Iyad bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If Satan comes to one of you while he is praying, So he said to him: You have spoken, so let him say: You lied as long as he does not smell its scent in his nose or hear its voice. By Your permission (Abu Dawud 1021, Ahmad 3/51)"
8081,"(8081) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: There is no ablution except from wind or sound. (Tirmidhi 75. Abu Dawud 179)"
8082,"(8082) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, who said: I saw Al-Sa'ib bin Khabab smelling his clothes, and I said to him: Why is that, may God have mercy on you? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: There is no ablution except from smell or hearing. (Ahmad 3/426, Tabarani 6622)"
8083,"(8083) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Qais bin Sakan, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: Satan comes to one of you while he is praying and causes his genitals to become wet until he sees that he has begun, and that He will come and hit his back, and show him that he has done it. So do not leave until you find a scent or find wetness."
8084,"(8084) Hushaym told us, he said: The common people told us, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymiy, he said: Abdullah said: Satan One of you comes while he is praying and taps his backside to show that he has performed the prayer. If he does that, then he does not One of you leaves until he hears a sound or feels a scent."
8085,"(8085) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A man asked him and he said to him: Satan comes to me while I am praying and whispers to me until he says: You have spoken. Then he said: He will not leave until He smells it, or hears it buzzing."
8086,"(8086) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, that he heard him say: Satan draws blood from a person, then he pulsates at his perineum and expels him, so none of you will come out until he hears. Feeling, or smelling."
8087,"(8087) Abbad told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He does not leave until he hears a voice, or finds A wind"
8088,"(8088) Hafs told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Shihr ibn Hawshab, who said: Satan will come to one of you and enter his nostrils. In his anus, he moves it and moves his genitals to spread, but they do not leave until he hears a sound or finds a scent."
8089,"(8089) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He used to say: Satan burrows into the urethra. Then it will pulsate at the anus, and the man will see that it has started, so none of you should leave until he hears a sound or feels a scent. Or he sees wetness."
8090,"(8090) Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: He does not leave until He hears a sound, or feels a smell."
8091,"(8091) Abu Asama told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, he said: Al-Minhal told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: Satan goes around the servant to cut off his prayers, but when he exhausts him, he blows on his backside and he does not leave until He hears a voice, or feels a smell, and comes to him and squeezes his penis and shows him that something has come out of it, but nothing He leaves until he is awake."
8092,"(8092) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abu Hurairah said: If one of you doubts about the calamity. While he is praying, let him place his hands on the pebbles, wipe one of them with the other, and continue with his prayer."
8093,"(8093) Mu’tamir narrated to us that he heard his father narrating: Zayd bin Thabit, Hudhayfi, Al-Hasan Al-Basri, and Ata’ did not They saw something wrong with the filth that a man found while he was praying, except that Ata’ said: Unless it is dripped. He said: And Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: And if it drops on your foot, he does not see it, and he does not have to return it or perform his ritual ablution."
8094,"(8094) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: A sheikh narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali: He asked Zayd bin Thabit about That is what he permitted."
8095,"(8095) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, who said: Hudhayfy was asked about the man who finds Wetness after ablution, and he said: I did not care if that happened after ablution, whether it was that or that, and he nodded. With his hand, what is in it?"
8096,"(8096) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, on the authority of al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I asked Sa`id ibn Al-Musayyab, Urwah bin Al-Zubayr, Sulaiman bin Yassar, and Abu Salma bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of a man whose semen came out So they all said: Send it down to the same level as the Qur’an. Whatever you know of it, wash it, and whatever of it overwhelms you, leave it."
8097,"(8097) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: : If your mother calls you to pray, answer her, and if your father calls you, do not answer him."
8098,"(8098) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If your mother calls you while you are in prayer So answer her, and if your father calls you, do not answer him until you have finished."
8099,"(8099) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, he said: I asked Mujahid, he said: I told him: Will the prayer be performed and you call your mother? He said: Answer your mother."
8100,"(8100) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam ibn Yahya, he said: Farqad al-Sabkhi narrated to us, on the authority of Murāh al-Tayyib, on the authority of Omar It is disliked for a man to pray with a shackle on his feet."
8101,"(8101) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Sa`id Ibn Abi Sadaqi, who said: I said to Ibn Sirin: If you sneeze in Prayer: What should I say? He said: Say: Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds."
8102,"(8102) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who sneezes during prayer, he said: Praise be to Him. God"
8103,"(8103) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan: What about a man sneezing during prayer? He said: Praise be to God in what is written and other than it."
8104,"(8104) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Al-Hakam Al-Sulami, who said: Between us, I am praying with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when a man from among the people sneezed, and I said: May God have mercy on you. Then the people lowered their gazes, and I said: What a burden to his mother. How do you look at me? He said: They began to beat their thighs with their hands, and when I saw them silence me, I remained silent, so when the Messenger of God prayed May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, may God bless him and grant him peace. I have never seen anyone like him before him or after him with better learning than him, by God. He did not hate me, nor curse me, nor hit me. He said: None of the people’s words are appropriate in this prayer. It is praising God, glorifying God, and reciting the Qur’an, or as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. (Muslim 381, Abu Dawud 927)"
8105,"(8105) Abd narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ghalib Abul-Dhudhail, who said: Abraham was asked about a man who sneezed during prayer. Then another said to him while he was praying: May God have mercy on you, and Abraham said: He only said what was fair and he does not have to repeat it."
8106,"(8106) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who sneezed while he was praying, and a man smelled him. While he was praying, he said: May God have mercy on you, and Abraham said: He will resume."
8107,"(8107) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jubair bin Shaybah, who said: I asked Sa’id bin A man who leaves alone performs tayammum and then finds water at a certain time? He said: Eid."
8108,"(8108) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: If he performs tayammum, then finds water at the time of prayer, he repeats it. Prayer"
8109,"(8109) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al Qasim, on the authority of his father; Concerning a man who performs tayammum and prays, then finds water at a certain time. He said: He will celebrate the Eid."
8110,"(8110) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who performs tayammum and then finds water, he said: He will repeat it."
8111,"(8111) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: He celebrates Eid."
8112,"(8112) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He celebrates the feast."
8113,"(8113) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, he said: He celebrates"
8114,"(8114) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If water falls at a certain time, he repeats the prayer."
8115,"(8115) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He celebrates the prayer."
8116,"(8116) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Bakr bin Sawadah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar: that two men They were both in state of ritual impurity, so they made orphans and prayed, then they reached water at a certain time, and one of them returned, but the other did not, so he mentioned that. To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: As for the one who repeated it, he will be rewarded twice, and as for the other one, it will be sufficient for him. His prayers (Abu Dawud 342. Daraqutni 2)"
8117,"(8117) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: A stranger blames what is between him and another. time. If he finds water, he performs ablution. If he does not find water, he performs tayammum and prays. If he finds water after that, he performs ablution and does not repeat it. Prayer"
8118,"(8118) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jubayr bin Shaybah, on the authority of Ibn Salama, on the authority of Abu Salama, He said: He will not celebrate Eid."
8119,"(8119) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He performed tayammum and prayed, then entered Medina in For a while he did not return."
8120,"(8120) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man performs tayammum, he prays, then comes to water. And at a time after he had finished his prayer, he had finished his prayer."
8121,"(8121) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no Eid, it has passed. His prayers"
8122,"(8122) Abdi told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab and al-Shu’bi, they said: If he prays for someone else If he kisses the qiblah, or does tayammum, or prays while there is blood or impurity on his garment, and then water enters the water at some other time, then he is not obligated to do so. Bring it back"
8123,"(8123) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he finds water, he may wash himself, and if he wishes, he may repeat it, and if If he wants, he will not return."
8124,"(8124) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: I was in company, and Ikrimah was in He was gentle, but there was no water with Ikrimah and his companions, so they performed tayammum and prayed. They came to the water, and Ikrimah said to them: You see? The sun on the top of the mountain? They said: No. He said: If you had seen it, we would not have done it again. Then tayammum was sufficient for us. So he said: So I set off until I entered the army and met Amr bin Muslim. He was a companion of a peacock, so I told him what Ikrimah said, so he went to a peacock and mentioned that to him, then he came back to me and said: I mentioned it to a peacock. What Ikrimah said, he said: He spoke the truth."
8125,"(8125) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Nabatiyah, who said: I heard Ibn Sirin say: I went out on a Hajj or Umrah journey. At the end of the night, I was afflicted with ritual impurity and we had no water, so I performed tayammum and prayed. When the morning prayer rose, a man said: O father. Did you repeat your prayer early? He said: If I had not found it for a hundred and twenty years, I would have repeated my prayer."
8126,"(8126) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of al-Makhwal, on the authority of Abu Saad, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: The Prophet passed by me. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while I was prostrating, I had braided my hair, so he loosened it, or he said: so he forbade me from doing so. (Abu Dawud 646; Abd al-Razzaq 2990)"
8127,"(8127) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab and Hudhayfah; Concerning a man praying while combing his hair. They mentioned a hadith other than that what it means is that they hated it."
8128,"(8128) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zuhair ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Aban ibn Uthman, he said: He saw Othman saw a man praying with his hair tied, and he said: O my nephew, the likeness of one who prays with his hair tied is like the one who prays. And he is hidden."
8129,"(8129) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: When Ibn Abbas prayed, his hair would fall to the ground."
8130,"(8130) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Abdullah: He entered the mosque and, lo, A man was praying with his hair tied, and when he left, Abdullah said: When you pray, do not tie your hair, for your hair prostrates with you and for you. There is a reward for every poetry. The man said: I am afraid that he will become accustomed to dust. So he said: Accumulating it is better for you."
8131,"(8131) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Farwa, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla used to weave His poetry, and when he prays, he spreads it out."
8132,"(8132) Ibn Fadil told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He used to dislike a man tying his hair during prayer."
8133,"(8133) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: A man should not pray while he is He is a man who recites his hair."
8134,"(8134) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that He said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to tie up any hair or clothing."
8135,"(8135) Shababā told us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The command of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was to prostrate over seven people, and he was commanded not to wrap one’s hair or clothes. (Bukhari 815, Abu Dawud 886)"
8136,"(8136) Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: We used not to perform ablution. From a place of resting place, and we do not wrap our hair or clothes during prayer."
8137,"(8137) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, on the authority of a scholar, who said: Al-Hasan bin Yazid used to see swords. So whenever the sword was brought to be seen while he was in the mosque, he would go out with it and look at it."
8138,"(8138) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Aslam al-Manqari, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza. Al-Khuza’i said: The sword should not be drawn in the mosque."
8139,"(8139) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He forbade or forbade drawing the sword in The mosque"
8140,"(8140) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, he heard Jabir say: A man passed through the mosque with a poison, and the Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Hold on to her blades. (Bukhari 7074, Muslim 121)"
8141,"(8141) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: If one of you passes by a arrow in the mosque, let him touch it by its blades. (Bukhari 452, Abu Dawud 2580)"
8142,"(8142) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you pass by a arrow, hold its blades."
8143,"(8143) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Suhaim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ma’abad, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, uncovered the curtain while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr, and said: O people, nothing remains of the glad tidings of the Prophethood except the good vision that a Muslim sees or it appears to him. I was forbidden to recite the Qur’an while bowing or prostrating."
8144,"(8144) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn told me, On the authority of his father, he said: I heard Ali, with the guidance of Kufa, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade his reciters. The Qur’an while I was kneeling. (Muslim 213. Ahmad 1/81)"
8145,"(8145) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Do not recite the Qur’an while you are bowing. Nor prostrating."
8146,"(8146) Ibn Idris and Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, who said: I recited the prostration while I was Prostrating, so I asked Saeed bin Jubayr and he said: It is sufficient for you, and why do you recite while you are prostrating?"
8147,"(8147) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no recitation in bowing or in prostration. They were appointed for the remembrance of God Almighty."
8148,"(8148) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Ali ibn Mudarik, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of al-Rabi` ibn Khuthaym, He said: Is any of you unable to recite a third of the Qur’an while bowing, or prostrating to God, the One and Only Eternal?"
8149,"(8149) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Aban ibn Sam`i, on the authority of a sheikh who was with Ibn al-Zubayr and he recited al-Baqarah while he was bowing, Then he raised his head and recited Al-Imran, then he prostrated and recited An-Nisa’, then he raised his head and recited Al-Ma’idah."
8150,"(8150) Ubaid bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Ubaid bin Umair used to recite in Bowing and prostration."
8151,"(8151) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He did not see any harm if a man was hasty, so he bowed and remained. He must recite one or two verses of the Surah while bowing."
8152,"(8152) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of his father, who said: I did not hear Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim mentioning Nothing of the matter of this world, except that I once heard him say: How many mosques do the orphans have?"
8153,"(8153) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, who said: I heard Zarra and Abu Wa’il say: A mosque built by so-and-so."
8154,"(8154) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He used to hate saying: A mosque built by so-and-so. He does not see any harm in saying: The prayer of the people of so-and-so."
8155,"(8155) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Jabir, that he said: I am the mosque of Muadh."
8156,"(8156) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The woman undergoing menstruation delays the afternoon prayer. She hastens the afternoon prayer, joins them together, performs a bath once, delays the sunset prayer, hastens the evening prayer, and performs a bath once. One time, and you wash yourself at dawn."
8157,"(8157) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Ikrimah: Concerning the mustahaadah, he said: It combines The two prayers"
8158,"(8158) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: If she wishes, let her combine them."
8159,"(8159) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, who heard Abu Salamah bin Abd al-Rahman say: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Do not let the Bedouins prevail over you in the name of your prayer, for it is only the evening prayer, and you only call upon it. The darkness is due to the darkness of the camels."
8160,"(8160) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Labid, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not let the Bedouins prevail over you regarding the name of your evening prayer, for it is... In the Book of God, it is the evening meal, and it is only covered by the milk of camels. (Muslim 2291, Ahmad 2/10)"
8161,"(8161) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, on the authority of a man he did not name, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not let the Bedouins prevail over you regarding the name of your evening prayer, for it is only in a book. God is the one who provides food, but he only provides protection with camels’ milk. (Abu Ali 865, Bayhaqi 372)"
8162,"(8162) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Rawwad narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Whenever Ibn Umar heard them They say that Al-Atama became very angry, or he strongly forbade."
8163,"(8163) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zaid bin Taman Abu Al-Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: He hated to Al-Atama says:"
8164,"(8164) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Fazara al-Absi, on the authority of Maymoon bin Mihran, who said: I said: To Abdullah bin Omar: Who was the first to name it Al-Atam? He said: Satan."
8165,"(8165) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Fazara, on the authority of Maimun, on the authority of Ibn Umar, with something similar."
8166,"(8166) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Sara, who said: I heard Salim saying: Do not say Al-‘Atamah is the last night’s dinner twice."
8167,"(8167) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hariz bin Uthman narrated to us, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Asim bin Hamid. Al-Sakouni, who was one of the companions of Muadh, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, said: We stayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the evening prayer. Then he came out to us and said: Follow this prayer, for you have been favored by it over all other nations, and no nation prayed it before you."
8168,"(8168) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him to Abu Bakr: When do you perform the Witr prayer? He said at the beginning of the night after dark, before I sleep."
8169,"(8169) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If your journey is one day in the dark, then do not The prayer should be shortened, so if it exceeds that, shorten it."
8170,"(8170) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, regarding his saying: {And do not be ungrateful. With your prayers and do not be afraid of them. She said: In supplications."
8171,"(8171) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid al-Mukhtab, on the authority of Ibrahim. On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ata’, they said: The supplications."
8172,"(8172) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, he said: His readers The Qur’an."
8173,"(8173) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Hijri, on the authority of Abu Iyad, who said: The supplications."
8174,"(8174) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: When God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recites, he raises his voice. This amazes the Muslims and is the worst of the infidels. He said, so it was revealed: {And do not speak loudly. With your prayers and do not be afraid of them}"
8175,"(8175) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’athi, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah He said: He who hears with my ears does not fear."
8176,"(8176) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Ubaydah about Qira’at? He said: Name yourself."
8177,"(8177) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said regarding the recitation of the day: Listen. Yourself"
8178,"(8178) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Hijri, on the authority of Abu Iyad, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace When he prayed at the House, he recited his recitation out loud, but the polytheists used to harm him, so it was revealed: (And do not be loud in your prayers, and do not be afraid With it (the verse)"
8179,"(8179) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: (And do not recite your prayers loudly. And do not be afraid of it.) He said: Supplication."
8180,"(8180) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Supplication."
8181,"(8181) Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyash Al-Amiri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, he said: It was Bedouins of Banu Tamim: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him, they said: O God, grant us wealth and children. Then (and do not be ungrateful) was revealed. With your prayers)"
8182,"(8182) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyash Al-Amiri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, something similar."
8183,"(8183) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: {And do not be emboldened. With your prayers and do not be afraid of them. He said: Be good in public and pass on in secret. Secret and public."
8184,"(8184) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Abu Sa’id narrated to us, saying: Salem narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id: {And do not be loud in your prayers. And do not be afraid of it. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to raise his voice in the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. His Muslim name was called the Most Merciful, so when the polytheists heard that from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, they would say: He mentioned He brought him to Al-Yamamah, then they opposed him with the bows, the chants, and the whistling, and God Almighty revealed: {And do not speak out loudly. With your prayers and do not be afraid of them}"
8185,"(8185) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham: That his father used to supplicate for Al-Zubair in his prayers. And he names her."
8186,"(8186) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Iyas, he said: Abu al-Darda’ said: I am praying for seventy of my brothers and I. prostrating"
8187,"(8187) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: That Ali used to name the men after the prayer."
8188,"(8188) Hushaym told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Atiya told us, he said: Tell me who saw Urwa bin Al-Zubair. And he prayed and said: O God, forgive Al-Zubair, O God, forgive Asma bint Abi Bakr."
8189,"(8189) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan. On the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, they both said: In your prayer, say whatever you wish to do."
8190,"(8190) Muadh told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I was informed that Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote that no one should be named in supplications."
8191,"(8191) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Al-Farafasi, he said: I heard Ibn Al-Zubair said while he was prostrating: Oh God, forgive Al-Zubair, O God, forgive Asma bint Abi Bakr Al-Siddiq."
8192,"(8192) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in saying in prayer: Oh God. Grant me a boy who will not be named."
8193,"(8193) Waki’ told us, he said: Ja’far bin Burqan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Marzuq, he said: Uthman said: It is not cut off. Prayer is nothing but speech and conversation."
8194,"(8194) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who speaks during prayer, and they said: If he speaks while... He finished his prayer and continued his prayer, and it had already ended, and upon him were the two prostrations of forgetfulness. And if he spoke and did not complete his prayer, then he should repeat it."
8195,"(8195) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He resumes."
8196,"(8196) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he spoke during the prayer, he would repeat the prayer. He did not perform ablution again."
8197,"(8197) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Harun, on the authority of Abu Sa’id: that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, traveled A farsakh to shorten the prayer. (Abdullah bin Hamid 947)"
8198,"(8198) Hushaym told us, he said: Juwaybir told us, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, on the authority of the fight: that Ali went out to the palm trees and prayed. He performed two rak'ahs at noon and afternoon, then he returned from his day and said: I wanted to teach you the Sunnah of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace."
8199,"(8199) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, he heard Anas say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. He performed the salutation in Medina at noon four times and in Dhul-Hulaifah two rak'ahs, meaning the afternoon prayer."
8200,"(8200) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Munkadir and Ibrahim bin Misra, they heard Anas say: I prayed four rak'ahs with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at noon in Medina and two rak'ahs at Dhu al-Hulaif. (Tirmidhi 546. Abu Dawud 1195)"
8201,"(8201) Waki’ told us, he said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Amer, he said: Whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out on a journey Shorten the prayer from Dhul-Halifah."
8202,"(8202) Abbad bin Al-Aam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim: that Hudhafi used to pray. Two rak'ahs between Kufa and Al-Mada'in."
8203,"(8203) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The prayer is shortened during His journey by day and night."
8204,"(8204) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zayd bin Khalidah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It should be shortened. Praying at a distance of three miles."
8205,"(8205) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Masruq used to shorten the prayer to a mediator."
8206,"(8206) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, he said: I went out with Masruq to the Silsilah. So he shortened the prayer and stayed there for two years, shortening the prayer and shortening it when he returned until he entered."
8207,"(8207) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Yahya ibn Yazid al-Hinai, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about He shortened the prayer and said: When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would set out a journey of three miles or three farsakhs. Shu'bah Al-Shak, pray two rak'ahs. (Muslim 12. Abu Dawud 1194)"
8208,"(8208) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus and Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The prayer is shortened during the two-night journey."
8209,"(8209) Hushaym told us, he said: Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: Al-Harith said to him: Should the prayer be shortened until... The cities? He said: Al-Mada'in is close, but to Ahwaz and the like."
8210,"(8210) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah’s companions were not negligent. To Wasit, Al-Mada'in and the like."
8211,"(8211) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Zakaria, that he heard Al-Sha’bi say: If I had traveled to the Foxes’ Monastery, I would have stopped short."
8212,"(8212) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Amir, the same, except that Waki’ said: If I had gone out."
8213,"(8213) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’athi, who said: It should be shortened in the course of six days. Miles"
8214,"(8214) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Salih and Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Suwayd. Ibn Ghaflali, he said: The prayer should be shortened in three journeys."
8215,"(8215) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, or someone else, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi: That it was He shortens the prayer to a mediator."
8216,"(8216) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Izzah, who said: I saw Al-Sha’bi shortening the prayer. To a mediator."
8217,"(8217) Wakī’ narrated to us, he said: Shu’bā narrated to us, on the authority of a man called Shubayl, on the authority of Abu Habră, he said: I said: To Ibn Abbas: Should I be shorter than the idiot? He said: Do you go and come back in one day? He said: I said: Yes, he said: No, except on an available day."
8218,"(8218) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn al-Ghaz narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He would not shorten the prayer except On the perfect day.
 Hisham said: I heard an alcoholic say something like that."
8219,"(8219) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If your travel is for a day in the dark, then do not You shorten the prayer, but if you exceed that, shorten the prayer."
8220,"(8220) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Salim: That Ibn Umar went out to a land of his own with the same monument, and he shortened it. It is sixteen farsakhs."
8221,"(8221) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ward, on the authority of Al-Lajlaj, he said: We were traveling with Omar bin The speaker will walk three miles, complete the prayer and break his fast."
8222,"(8222) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Al-Ghaz told us, on the authority of Rabi’a Al-Jarshi, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, he said : I said to Ibn Abbas: Should I go to Arafah? He said: No, I said: Should I shorten it to Murr? He said: No, I said should I shorten it to Taif and Usfan? He said: Yes, and that is forty-eight miles, and he held it in his hand."
8223,"(8223) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I will travel on an hour from The day is shorter."
8224,"(8224) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, he said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Do not limit yourself to what you know. And a middle of palm trees, and go as far as Usfan, Taif, and Jidda, and when you come to meet people or livestock, complete it."
8225,"(8225) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Jabir bin Zayd said to me: Shorten your hair according to your custom."
8226,"(8226) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Should I shorten my knowledge? He said: No."
8227,"(8227) Ubaid bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Yazid bin Khumir, who said: I heard Habib bin Ubaid He narrates, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Ibn Al-Samt, who said: I witnessed Omar in Dhul-Halif as if he wanted to pray to Mecca. You prayed two rak'ahs, so I said to him: Why are you doing this? He said: I am only doing what I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing. (Muslim 481. Ahmad 1/30)"
8228,"(8228) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Khaythamiya, he said: Al-Harith bin Qais Al-Ju’fi went out, and when he left Houses shorten the prayer. He said: Then it was said to him: Shorten the prayer. He said, “Complete it today and shorten it tomorrow.”"
8229,"(8229) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid al-Fayshi, who said: We went out with Ali to Siffin, pray two rak'ahs between the bridge and the bridge."
8230,"(8230) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whenever a pilgrim went out as a pilgrim, he would enter ihram from Najaf and shorten his prayers."
8231,"(8231) Muadh told us: Ibn Juraij told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The prayer is shortened on the complete day. And do not fall short in anything other than that."
8232,"(8232) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Imran bin Umair, on the authority of his father, who said: I went out with Abdullah to He went to Mecca and prayed two rak'ahs at the Qantara Al-Hira."
8233,"(8233) Muhammad bin Fudayl and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Zaid said: Abdullah said: Prayer should not be shortened except during Hajj or Jihad."
8234,"(8234) Waki’ told us, he said: Mis’ar and Sufyan told us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: He told me Ibn Masoud: Do not let your blackness deceive you from your prayers, for it is only part of your kufa."
8235,"(8235) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaab, who said: A man who recited the book of Uthman or who read it narrated to me. Ali, and he said: Now, I have been informed that some men among you will go out to their camps, either in gatherings or in collecting taxes. Either in their business they shorten the prayer or they do not complete the prayer, so do not do that. Rather, the prayer is shortened by one who is staring or In the presence of an enemy."
8236,"(8236) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, he said: Ibrahim al-Taymi would not see the palace except during Hajj or Jihad. Or a lifetime."
8237,"(8237) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They used to say: The journey during which the prayer is shortened. The one in which food and supplies are carried."
8238,"(8238) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, He said: Do not let this blackness of yours deceive you from your prayers, for it is from your Egypt."
8239,"(8239) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Farwa, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father: that Mu’adh Uqaba bin Amir and Ibn Masoud said: Do not let your livestock deceive you. One of you steps on the humps of the mountains with your livestock, or The stomachs of valleys and you claim that you are a traveler with no honor or honour. Rather, negligence is in the constant journey from one horizon to the next."
8240,"(8240) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Omar, who said: The travel prayer is two rak’ahs. Completely, without limiting it to the words of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
8241,"(8241) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Shafi, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: We are a people who were When we traveled, we had with us some of our servants who were sufficient to serve us, so how should we pray? He said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was traveling, he would pray two rak’ahs until he returned. He said: Then I came back and asked him, and he said: Like that, then I returned and some of the people said to me: Do you not understand? Do you not listen to what he is telling you? (Ahmad 1/241, Tabarani 12712)"
8242,"(8242) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Hanzali, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about prayer while travelling. He said: Two rak'ahs of the Sunnah of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmad 2/135)"
8243,"(8243) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ammar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Baba, on the authority of Ali ibn Umayyah, he said: I asked Omar ibn Al-Khattab, saying: {There is no blame on you if you shorten the prayer if you fear that those who They disbelieved} and the people believed, so he said: I am amazed at what you marveled at. So I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and he said: He spoke the truth. God has given it to you in charity, so accept His charity. (Muslim 4. Abu Dawud 1192)"
8244,"(8244) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Laila, who said: Salman went out with thirteen men from The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Salman invaded them. When the time for prayer came, they said to him: Come forward, O father. Abdullah, and he said: I am not the one who advances while you are Arabs among you, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so let some of you advance. Then some of the people came forward and he led them in prayer with four rak’ahs. When we finished the prayer, Salman said: And what is for the square? It was enough for us. Two rak'ahs of half the square."
8245,"(8245) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Ubaid Al-Tai narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’i Al-Walabi, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin We lost him, he said: We set out on a journey and we were twelve or thirteen riders, all of whom accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him and others, said: Then the time for prayer came, and the people jostled, and a young man among them came forward, and he led them in four rak’ahs, and when he prayed Salman said: What do we have with the square? Half of the square is enough for us. We are poorer to reduce it. So they said: You come forward, O Abu. Abdullah led us in detail and said: You are the sons of Ishmael, the Imams, and we are the ministers."
8246,"(8246) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I am a merchant who went to Bahrain, so he ordered him to pray. Two rak'ahs"
8247,"(8247) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I asked Salma bin Suhayb while we were in Sijistan about prayer, and he said: Pray two rak'ahs until you return to your family, this is what Abdullah bin Masoud used to say."
8248,"(8248) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: We prayed. With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, between Mecca and Medina, and we are safe, not afraid of anything. (Tirmidhi 547. Ahmad 1/226)"
8249,"(8249) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Awn bin Abi Juhayfah Al-Sawa’i, on the authority of His father, he said: I prayed two rak’ahs with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, at noon prayer. Then he continued to pray two rak’ahs. Until he returned to Medina. (Ahmad 4/309. Tabarani 251)"
8250,"(8250) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The first time it was imposed The prayer consisted of two rak'ahs, then it was increased and made four for the resident. (Bukhari 350, Muslim 478)"
8251,"(8251) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mas’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Sammak al-Hanafi, saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The two rak’ahs when traveling. Complete, not short."
8252,"(8252) Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Waqa’ ibn Iyas, on the authority of Ali ibn Rabi’i: that Ali went out on a journey and was praying. Two rak'ahs until he returns."
8253,"(8253) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Harb bin Abi Al-Aswad: that Ali came out of Al-Basra, so he prayed four rak'ahs, then said: When we pass this portion, we will pray two rak'ahs."
8254,"(8254) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, that he heard a man asking Sa’id bin al-Musayyab: “Complete Praying and fasting while travelling? He said: No. He said: I am stronger for that. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was stronger than you. He used to fall short. Praying while traveling and breaking the fast, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best of you is he who shortens the prayer while traveling and breaks his fast. (Abdul Razzaq 4480, Tabarani 6554)"
8255,"(8255) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I met Abdullah bin Maqil in Al-Madain and said: He is the imam of my people. I want to return to my family, so how much should I pray? He said: Four, then I met him after that and said: I want to return to my family. How much do you command me to pray? He said: Two rak'ahs."
8256,"(8256) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Nafi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, he said: My father was He shortens his hair from the time he leaves his house until he returns to his family."
8257,"(8257) Hushaym told us, saying: Haroun bin Zarawa told us, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas, and he said: I and a companion of mine were on a journey, and I was completing my duties, but my companion was falling short. Ibn Abbas said to him: Rather, you are the one who was You fell short while your companion who was performing the prayer did so."
8258,"(8258) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, who said: Imran Ibn Husayn passed in our gathering. Then a young man from the people came up to him and asked him about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during Hajj, the Battle of the Battle of God, and the Umrah. Then he came and stood over us and said: This man asked me about a matter and I wanted you to hear it, or as he said: I fought with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He did not pray except two rak’ahs until he returned to Medina, and I performed Hajj with him, and he did not pray except two rak’ahs. Until he returned to Medina, and I witnessed the conquest with him, so he stayed in Mecca for eighteen nights, praying only two rak’ahs. He said to the people of the town: Pray four times, for we are on a journey. I performed Umrah with him for three years, and he did not pray except two rak’ahs, and I performed Hajj with my father. Bakr and I performed Hajj and he did not pray except two rak’ahs until he returned to Medina. I performed Hajj with Omar and he did not pray except two rak’ahs. Until he returned to Medina, and she performed Hajj with Othman for seven years of his rule, praying only two rak’ahs, then he prayed with Uthman. Four"
8259,"(8259) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfy, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the two rak’ahs of a traveler’s prayer at noon in Mecca."
8260,"(8260) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazaid, who said: Othman prayed. Four rak'ahs in Mina, and Abdullah said: I prayed two rak'ahs with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and two rak'ahs with Abu Bakr. And with Omar I prayed two rak'ahs, then your paths separated, and I wished that of the four rak'ahs I had two rak'ahs that would come to me.
(Bukhari 1457, Muslim 19)"
8261,"(8261) Abu Bakr bin Ayash and Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Wahb Al-Khuza’i, He said: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a safe place as long as the people were, and I performed two rak’ahs as often as possible. (Bukhari 1083, Muslim 21)"
8262,"(8262) Waki’ told us, he said: Saeed bin Al-Sa’ib Al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Asim Al-Thaqafi, he said: I asked Ibn Omar Concerning the prayer at Minna, he said: Have you heard of Muhammad and believed in him? He used to pray two rak’ahs at Minna. (Ahmed 2/24)"
8263,"(8263) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Omar And Othman left his emirate. They prayed two rak'ahs at Mina."
8264,"(8264) Waki’ told us, he said: Hanzala told us, he said: I asked Al-Qasim, Salim, and Tawus about the prayer in Mina, and they said: Shorten it."
8265,"(8265) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The traveler prays two rak’ahs until he returns, unless He comes to one of the countries and performs their prayers."
8266,"(8266) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha: The first prayer to be made obligatory was two rak’ahs. So the urban prayer was increased and the travel prayer was approved, so I said to Urwah: What was the matter with Aisha, who used to complete the prayer while traveling? Do you say this? He said: She interpreted what Othman interpreted, so I did not ask him what Othman interpreted. (Muslim 678)"
8267,"(8267) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah ibn Umar, who said: I was informed on the authority of al-Qasim and Salim that they used to say: When the people of Mecca go to Mina, they shorten their prayers.
 He said: Ata’ and Al-Zuhri used to say: They complete."
8268,"(8268) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He used to reside in Mecca. So when he leaves for Mina, he stops."
8269,"(8269) Ubaidullah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hanzala, he said: I asked Al-Qasim about praying with the imam according to your knowledge? He said: Pray as he prayed.
 He said: I asked Salim and Tawoos and they said something like that."
8270,"(8270) Ubayd Allah bin Uthman bin Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata, who said: The people of Mecca do not have to shorten the prayer. In Hajj"
8271,"(8271) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mughirah bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to complete the prayer while traveling, shorten the prayer, fast, break the fast, delay the noon prayer, hasten the afternoon prayer, and delay the sunset prayer. And he hastens the evening meal. (Daraqutni 45. Tahawi 164)"
8272,"(8272) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalābāb, who said: If you pray two rak’ahs while traveling, then it is according to the Sunnah, and if I prayed four times according to the Sunnah."
8273,"(8273) Abdā narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha: She used to complete the prayer while travelling."
8274,"(8274) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Khudair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Najih al-Makki, who said: Companions accompanied The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey, and some of them would complete it, some of them would shorten their prayers, and some of them would fast. And some of them break the fast, so these people do not blame others, nor do these people blame others."
8275,"(8275) Waki’ told us, he said: Bastam bin Muslim told us, he said: I asked Ata’ about shortening the prayer while travelling? He said: If you fall short, then make it easy, and if you wish, you can complete it."
8276,"(8276) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Habib bin Shahid, on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran, that he asked Saeed bin The one who abandons prayer while traveling, and he said: If you wish, perform two rak’ahs, and if you wish, then four."
8277,"(8277) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: I said to them: A man’s ten days seem shorter. Prayer? He said: They said: No."
8278,"(8278) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, who said: Jabir bin Zayd was asked about the people. They set off from Egypt to the wilderness, performing two prayers as long as they started until they return to Egypt? He said: No, to complete the prayer near and far, as long as they are beginning."
8279,"(8279) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ali ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abu Nazra, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn, he said: I witnessed with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conquered the conquest and stayed in Mecca for eighteen nights, praying only two rak’ahs, then He says to the people of the town: Pray four times, for we are on a journey."
8280,"(8280) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed at the conquest of Mecca for fifteen days, shortening the prayer until he went to Hunayn. (Abu Dawud 1224. An-Nasa’i 511)"
8281,"(8281) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, who said: I heard Anas bin Malik say: We left. With the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he shortened the prayer until we came to Mecca, and he stayed there ten times, shortening the prayer until he returned to... Medina (Bukhari 1081, Muslim 15)"
8282,"(8282) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn al-Asbaani, on the authority of Ikrimah: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed in Mecca. Seventeen days of shortening the prayer."
8283,"(8283) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Simak bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If you reside in the land of five Take a few months and shorten the prayer."
8284,"(8284) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar and Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Miswar. He said: We stayed with Saad bin Malik for two months. Sufyan said: In Amman, and Mas’ar said: In Amman, or Amman, shortening the prayer. And we did so, so we told him, and he said: We know best."
8285,"(8285) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah al-Dab’i, on the authority of a man from Anazi whose nickname was Abu Al-Minhal, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: I am staying in Medina for a year and I do not find it difficult to walk. He said: Pray two rak’ahs."
8286,"(8286) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Muthanna bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Jamra Nasr bin Imran, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: We are prolonging the invasion of Khorasan, so what do you think? He said: Pray two rak'ahs, even if you stay in prayer for twenty years."
8287,"(8287) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: that Abdul-Rahman bin Samarra spent the winter in Kabul, or He prays two rak'ahs in winter."
8288,"(8288) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Anas bin Malik stayed in Sabur for a year or two, praying. Two rak'ahs, then he says the salutation, then he prays two rak'ahs."
8289,"(8289) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Malik, who said: I said to Jabir bin Zayd: I will perform the one and two years in Kaskar. And I am similar to the family, so he said: Pray two rak’ahs."
8290,"(8290) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Masruq, who said: I stayed with him for two years and he prayed two rak’ahs. With the chain, he said: I said to him: What made you do this, Abu Aisha? He said: Seeking the Sunnah."
8291,"(8291) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of something similar."
8292,"(8292) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I was with Alqamiya in Khwarazm for two years, praying. Two rak'ahs"
8293,"(8293) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Ibn Thawban said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed in Tabuk for twenty nights, praying the prayer of a traveler. Two rak'ahs (Bayhaqi 152. Abdul Razzaq 4335)"
8294,"(8294) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, who said: Alqamiya stayed after two years in the battle, but he fell short. Prayer"
8295,"(8295) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, established seven He shortens the prayer for the first ten days. He said: Ibn Abbas said: Whoever performs the iqama for seventeen days, shortens the prayer, and whoever performs more than that will complete the prayer. (Bukhari 1080 and Abu Dawud 1223)"
8296,"(8296) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: If a man agrees on Iqamah for fifteen days, complete the prayer."
8297,"(8297) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, he said: If you perform ten days, complete them."
8298,"(8298) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, something similar."
8299,"(8299) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of his father, who said: Whoever performs ten days of prayer will complete it."
8300,"(8300) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, that he used to complete the prayer on the ten days of prayer."
8301,"(8301) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Dharr narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When Ibn Omar agreed upon the establishment of five He left his afternoon and prayed four times."
8302,"(8302) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: If you stay longer Fifteen days ago, he completed the prayer."
8303,"(8303) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: If you stay in prayer for four, pray four."
8304,"(8304) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Quray bin Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hakimah, he said: I asked Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, and he said: If you stand for three days, complete the prayer."
8305,"(8305) Waki’ said: I heard Sufyan saying: If there is consensus at the place of fifteen days, he should complete the prayer when he enters, and if there is no When he comes out, pray two rak'ahs, and if he stays for a year, that is the saying with him."
8306,"(8306) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Aisha, who said: If you put in the provisions and the auction, separate Four, and when Tawoos came to Mecca, he would pray four."
8307,"(8307) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu al-A’liyah, who said: He prays two rak’ahs, and when he is at ease, he prays Four, meaning when it descends."
8308,"(8308) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If you finish your livestock So he completed it."
8309,"(8309) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, like him."
8310,"(8310) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a traveler arrives from another country in Egypt, he prays four times."
8311,"(8311) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father: That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was If the journey is serious, combine Maghrib and Isha. (Bukhari 1106. Muslim 45)"
8312,"(8312) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, eight all and seven all. He said: I said: O Abu Al-Sha’atha’, I think he delayed the afternoon and hastened the afternoon and delayed Maghrib and hastened the evening prayer. He said: I think so. (Bukhari 543, Abu Dawud 1207)"
8313,"(8313) Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered May the peace and blessings of God be upon him in his invasion of Tabuk between noon and afternoon and between sunset and evening."
8314,"(8314) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abu al-Tufayl, on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, combined the noon and afternoon prayers and the sunset and evening prayers when traveling during his expedition to Tabuk. (Muslim 52. Abu Dawud 1199)"
8315,"(8315) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Dawud bin Qais Al-Fara’i narrated to us, on the authority of Salih, the guardian of the twins, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered the noon, afternoon, sunset and evening prayers in Medina without fear or Matar, he said: Then it was said to Ibn Abbas: Why did he do that? He said: He wanted to expand his nation. (Ahmad 1/346, Abu Ali 2670)"
8316,"(8316) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq al-Uqaili, who said: A man said To Ibn Abbas: The prayer, but he remained silent. Then he said to him: The prayer, so he remained silent. Then he said to him: The prayer is three times, so he said: There is no mother for you. You teach us. With prayer, we used to combine the two prayers at the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, meaning when travelling. (Muslim 58. Ahmad 351)"
8317,"(8317) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Hafs bin Ubaid Allah bin Anas, who said: We were travelling. With Anas bin Malik. When the sun went down while he was at home, he would not ride until he had prayed the noon prayer. When he went, Then the afternoon prayer came and he prayed the afternoon prayer, but if he walked from his house before the sun passed and the prayer came, we said to him: The prayer, and he said: Walk. Even when it was between the two prayers, he descended and combined the noon and afternoon prayers, then he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, when he joined his purity with his spirit, he did this and that. (Abdul Razzaq 4395)"
8318,"(8318) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: Ibn Abbas came from Taif and delayed the Maghrib prayer. Then he came down and combined the evening prayer with the evening prayer."
8319,"(8319) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: Saad and I went out to Mecca, and he was gathering among The two prayers between Dhuhr and Asr. He delays this, and hastens that, and prays them together, and delays Maghrib. He hastens the evening prayer, then they all pray together until we reach Mecca."
8320,"(8320) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Habib bin Shihab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: I accompanied him in Traveling, he used to combine between noon and afternoon prayers and between sunset and evening prayers."
8321,"(8321) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: I traveled with Asama bin Zaid and Sa’id bin Zaid, and they used to gather together between noon and afternoon, sunset and evening."
8322,"(8322) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abd al-Jalil bin Atiyya, who said: I traveled with Jabir bin Zaid, and he was He combines the two prayers."
8323,"(8323) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mugheerah bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to delay the noon prayer and hasten the afternoon prayer, delay the sunset prayer, and hasten the evening prayer while traveling."
8324,"(8324) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Hudhayl bin Shurahbil Al-Awdi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined the noon, afternoon, sunset and evening prayers in travel. (Tayalisi 376)"
8325,"(8325) Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazeed. On the authority of Abdullah, he said: I did not see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying a prayer except at its appointed time, except for the evening prayer. And the Maghrib prayer, for he joined them together on that day, and prayed Fajr that day before its appointed time. (Bukhari 1482 and Abu Dawud 1929)"
8326,"(8326) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: When Osama bin Zayd used to travel in haste, Combine the two prayers."
8327,"(8327) Waki’ told us, he said: Malik bin Mughul told us, he said: I asked Ata’ about delaying the noon and sunset times. Traveling, but he did not see any harm in it."
8328,"(8328) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zaid Abi Asama, who said: I asked Mujahid about delaying the Maghrib prayer and hastening the evening prayer. While traveling, he did not see any harm in it."
8329,"(8329) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of May God bless him and grant him peace between the two prayers during the invasion of Banu Mutaliq. (Ahmed 179)"
8330,"(8330) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather: that Ali was He prays the Maghrib prayer while traveling, then he has dinner, then he performs the evening prayer after that, then he says: This is how I saw the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. (Abu Dawud 1227. An-Nasa’i 1571)"
8331,"(8331) Bakr bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, saying: Issa bin Al-Mukhtar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Qays. On the authority of Huzail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined the two prayers while travelling. (Tabarani 9881, Abu Ali 5413)"
8332,"(8332) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Al-Aswad and his companions were camping At the time of each prayer while traveling, they pray Maghrib at its time, then they have dinner, then they stay for an hour, then they pray Dinner"
8333,"(8333) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayy bin Abdullah, who said: The letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz came to us: that you should not combine Between the two prayers, except for an excuse."
8334,"(8334) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about combining the two prayers while traveling, but he said no. He likes that, except for an excuse."
8335,"(8335) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim: that the lions used to descend during the time of prayer. When traveling, even if it is on a stone."
8336,"(8336) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: It was nothing but When the time for prayer came, he would descend, even if it was on a stone."
8337,"(8337) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Hilal narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzali al-Sadusi, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The combination of Two prayers without an excuse are major sins."
8338,"(8338) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Omar, He said: Combining two prayers without an excuse is a major sin."
8339,"(8339) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawāhib narrated to us, saying: I came safely and said, O father What age do you have to combine the two prayers while travelling? He said: No, unless a journey hastens me."
8340,"(8340) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: It was mentioned to Muhammad ibn Sirin that Jabir ibn Zayd combined The two prayers, and he said: I do not think that he should combine the two prayers except for a matter of command."
8341,"(8341) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: We do not know of the Sunnah to combine The two prayers are in the city or on the road, except between noon and afternoon, according to custom, and between sunset and isha, combined."
8342,"(8342) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala: That a man came to Sa`id bin al-Musayyab and said: I asked a camel herder to pray the Maghrib prayer in the evening, then I laid down and lay down in the darkness, and he said: Do not sleep until You pray for her, and if you fear that she will sleep, then join them together."
8343,"(8343) Abdullah bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Ya’qub, on the authority of Ata’, and on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak in a sick person praying. They said: If he wishes, he can combine the two prayers."
8344,"(8344) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ya’qub, on the authority of Ata’ about a shepherd who falls short. He said: It is only the traveler who falls short."
8345,"(8345) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, and Abi Al-Bakhtari, he said: I think And their companions said: When two armies meet and people strike one another and the time for prayer comes, say: Glory be to God and praise be to God. There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest, so that is your prayer, then do not repeat it."
8346,"(8346) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid and Al-Hakam, who said: If he is at the battle cruiser and at the swords’ drawers, the man is sufficient. That his prayer be a takbeer, and if it is only one takbeer, then it is sufficient wherever his face is."
8347,"(8347) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: In the words of God Almighty: {Then if you fear, then on foot or mounted} He said: Then Prayer is approaching while you are being chased, so face wherever your face is and make the prostration lower than the bowing."
8348,"(8348) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Abu Muslimama, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Jabir bin Ghurab, who was the master of the tiger, he said We were with Harim bin Hayyan in an army fighting the enemy, and Harim said: Let every man among you prostrate under the garden."
8349,"(8349) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he was asked about a man who, when the distances approach, how should he pray? He said: He prays in two rak'ahs and two prostrations facing him."
8350,"(8350) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about the prayer of distances, and they said: Raka’ah. Where his face was nodding."
8351,"(8351) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’bā narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirā, on the authority of Abraham, who said: Praying at a distance is one rak’ah. He nods wherever his face was."
8352,"(8352) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It is sufficient to say takbeerah. At the basket if he is not able."
8353,"(8353) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he used to say in the Musafi prayer: He gestures gesturing. Where his face was."
8354,"(8354) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: Two takbeers at Al-Musayafa"
8355,"(8355) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Praying at a distance is two rak’ahs."
8356,"(8356) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Raja` ibn Huywah al-Kindi, who said: Thabit ibn al-Samit narrated, Or Al-Samt bin Thabit, who was walking in fear, and the time for prayer came, so they prayed in two mounts, and Al-Ashtar came down and said: What’s wrong with him? They said: He came down and prayed. He said: He has no other reason to disagree with him."
8357,"(8357) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Jaham bin Sukhair Al-Adawi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the prayer of fear With Dhu Qard, land from the land of Banu Sulaym, so the people lined up behind him in two rows, lined up behind him, and lined up parallel to the enemy, so he prayed in a row. He bowed down, then these people bowed down to the rows of these, and these to the rows of these, and he prayed with them. Rakaa (Ahmad 1/232; Abd al-Razzaq 357)"
8358,"(8358) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukn Al-Fazari, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Hassan, on the authority of Zaid bin It is proven that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the prayer of fear.
 Sufyan said, and he mentioned something like the hadith of Ibn Abbas. (Nasa’i 1919. Ibn Khuzaymah 1345)"
8359,"(8359) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Tha’labah Ibn Zadam Al-Hanzali, he said: We were with Saeed Ibn Al-Aas in Tabaristan and Hudhayfah was with us, so Saeed said: Which of you prayed with me? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the prayer of fear? He said: Hudhayfah: I. He said: So he stood up and led the people in prayer.
 Sufyan said: He mentioned something like the hadith of Ibn Abbas and Zayd bin Thabit. (Abu Dawud 1240. Ahmad 5/399)"
8360,"(8360) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah Al-Rihahi: that Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari was in the house from Asbahan, and there was not a lot of fear in them at that time, but he wanted to teach them their religion. And the example of their Prophet, so he put them in two ranks, a group with weapons, approaching its enemy, and a group behind them, so he prayed. With those who recite it in a bow, then they turn on their backs until they stand in the place of the others, and they penetrate them until they stand behind him. So he led them in another rak'ah of prayer, then he gave the salutation. Then those following stood up and the others prayed one rak'ah after another, and some of them saluted them. On some, the imam completed two rak'ahs in congregation, and one rak'ah for the people. (Tabarani 197 Bayhaqi 253)"
8361,"(8361) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed for us. May God bless him and grant him peace. He prayed in fear, so they stood in two rows, a line behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a row facing the enemy, so he prayed. With them, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, bowed and the others came and stood in their place, and he faced the enemy and led them in prayer. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, bowed, then gave the salutation. Then these people stood up and prayed one rak’ah for themselves, then gave the salutation, then They went and took their place in the face of the enemy, and they returned to their place and prayed a rak'ah for themselves, then they saluted. (Abu Dawud 1237, Ahmad 375)"
8362,"(8362) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Zaid Al-Faqir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he led them in prayer with the prayer of fear, so he stood in a row in front of him and a row behind him, so he led them in prayer, and those came. Until they stood in the place of those, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the prayer with them, bowing and prostrating, then he saluted, and it was The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, has two rak’ahs, and for them there is one rak’ah. (Nasa’i 1933. Ahmad 3/298)"
8363,"(8363) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Dharr narrated to us that he heard it from a mujahid who said: The Messenger of God was in Usfan and the polytheists. With great anger, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the noon prayer, the polytheists saw him bowing and prostrating, so they decided to They attacked him, and when the afternoon prayer came, the people lined up in two rows behind him, so he said “Allahu Akbar” and they all said “Allahu Akbar” and he bowed and they all bowed and prostrated. The second row prostrated, and the second row stood up, those with their weapons, approaching the enemy with their faces straight. When the Prophet rose, he prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. The second row prostrated, and when they raised their heads, he bowed, and they all bowed, and he prostrated, and the row of his color prostrated. The second row stood up with their weapons, facing the enemy with their faces. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his head, the row prostrated. The second
 He said: Mujahid said, so their takbeer, bowing, and greetings were all equal, and they took equal parts in prostration. He said: Mujahid said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray the prayer of fear before his day, nor after it. (Abdul Razzaq 4235)"
8364,"(8364) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Ayyash al-Zarqi, on the authority of the Prophet"
8365,"(8365) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said the salaam with something like the hadith of Mujahid, and added to it, as these guards of yours do to their commanders. (Muslim 308. Ahmad 3/374)"
8366,"(8366) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed They performed two rak'ahs, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had two rak'ahs, and for them there was one rak'ah."
8367,"(8367) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi and Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid al-Faqir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The fear prayer is one rak'ah, one rak'ah."
8368,"(8368) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awana, on the authority of Bukair ibn al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: God Almighty made it obligatory for the home prayer to be four rak’ahs, for traveling to be two rak’ahs, and for fear to be two rak’ahs, according to the tongue of your Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted you. (Muslim 479. Abu Dawud 1241)"
8369,"(8369) Qasim bin Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Aidh, on the authority of Bukair bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: God made it obligatory for the urban prayer to be four rak’ahs, the traveling prayer to be two rak’ahs, and the fear prayer to be four rak’ahs, according to the tongue of His Prophet, or your Prophet said. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Muslim 479. Ahmad 1/243)"
8370,"(8370) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the prayer of fear during some of his days, and a group rose up with him and a group against the enemy. He led those with him in prayer with one rak'ah, then they went and the others came and he led them in prayer with one rak'ah, then the two groups performed one rak'ah. Rakaa
 He said: Ibn Umar said: If the fear is greater than that, pray while riding or standing, gesturing. (Bukhari 943. Muslim 306)"
8371,"(8371) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: I prayed the prayer of fear. He prayed two rak'ahs with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, except for Maghrib, in which he prayed three rak'ahs."
8372,"(8372) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he was asked about the prayer of fear, and he said: It was reported on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led his companions and prayed with a group of them, and another group faced the enemy and he prayed. He performed two rak'ahs with them, then they stood in the place of the others, and the others came and prayed. He performed two rak'ahs with them, then he greeted them. (Nasa’i 1942. Bayqaqi 259)"
8373,"(8373) Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban bin Zaid narrated: Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: We came with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, even when we were in the same place. The call to prayer was called, and he prayed two rak’ahs in one group, then they delayed and he prayed two rak’ahs with the other group. He said: It was for the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, four rak’ahs, and two rak’ahs for the people. (Muslim 311. Ibn Hibban 2884)"
8374,"(8374) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sulaym ibn Abd, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: The prayer of fear is two rak’ahs. And four prostrations. If the enemy hastens you, fighting and talking between the two rak’ahs is permissible for you."
8375,"(8375) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sulaym bin Abd al-Saluli, on the authority of Hudhayf He said: If someone attacks you, then fighting and speaking are permissible for you, meaning prayer."
8376,"(8376) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: that Abu Musa led his companions in prayer in Isbaan, and a group of people prayed. He and a group of them were with him, facing the enemy, and he prayed with them in bowing, then they bowed down and the others came and interspersed with them, so he prayed. He bowed with them, then said the salaam, and the two groups stood up and prayed one rak'ah after another."
8377,"(8377) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, he heard Jabir say: He was asked about the fear prayer? He said: As these princes of yours do."
8378,"(8378) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I heard him narrating, on the authority of Abu Ayash. Al-Zarqi: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was in line with the enemy in Usfan, and Khalid bin Al-Walid was against the polytheists, so he led them in prayer. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then the polytheists said: They will have a prayer after this that is more beloved to them than Their wealth and their children. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led them in prayer and arranged them in two rows behind him. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bowed down with them all, and when they raised their heads, the next row prostrated, and the others stood up. When they raised their heads from prostration, the back row prostrated as they bowed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Then the row fell behind. The front row advanced and the back row advanced for their kneeling with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the back row fell behind and the front row advanced. So each one of them stood in the place of his companion, then he bowed and the others stood up, and when they finished their prostration the others prostrated, then the Prophet saluted. May God’s prayers and peace be upon them. (Nasa’i 1937. Ahmad 4/60)"
8379,"(8379) Yazid bin Harun told us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Salih bin Khawat. On the authority of Sahil bin Abi Hatham, regarding the fear prayer, he said: The imam stands towards the qiblah, and a group of people is with him, and a group is facing him. Then the enemy leads in prayer with those who are with him, bowing, and when he stands, he stands upright, and those behind him lead the prayer for themselves, bowing, prostrating, and giving salutations, then They went to take the place of their brothers who were facing the enemy, and the others returned on their heels, so they stood behind the imam, and he led them in prayer. He bowed another bow, then he gave the salutation, and those behind them stood up and bowed for themselves, prostrated and saluted. (Bukhari 4131, Abu Dawud 1232)"
8380,"(8380) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, who said: What is the rak’ah like? Shortened while they were praying two rak'ahs."
8381,"(8381) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Masruq, that he said: The prayer of fear is established. The Imam and they line up two rows behind him, then the Imam kneels, and those next to him kneel, then he prostrates with those next to him, and lo! Those of his color fell behind, and the others came and stood in their place. He kneeled with them and prostrated with them while the others stood, then They will stand up and perform one rak'ah after another, and the imam will have two rak'ahs in congregation, and the people will have one rak'ah after another rak'ah. in congregation and perform the second rak’ah."
8382,"(8382) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, for example That"
8383,"(8383) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Ansari. Uqba bin Amr said: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people said: It only eclipsed due to his death. Abraham, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The sun and the moon are not eclipsed due to the death of anyone or his life, but they They are two signs of God, so when you see them, pray. (Bukhari 1041, Muslim 23)"
8384,"(8384) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir: That the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed in an eclipse similar to your prayer, bowing and prostrating. (Abu Dawud 1186. Ahmad 4/267)"
8385,"(8385) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: It collapsed. The sun was at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he stood up and we stood up with him. Then he said: O people, the sun and the moon are two signs. Of the signs of God, so when one of them collapses, run to the mosques. (Nasa’i 1867)"
8386,"(8386) Ibn Aliyah and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He prayed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us during a solar eclipse, eight rak’ahs in four prostrations. (Muslim 18. Abu Dawud 1176)"
8387,"(8387) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He acknowledged something similar, but did not mention Ibn Abbas."
8388,"(8388) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He prayed, and he finished his prayer when he emerged from the sun. He thanked and praised God, then he said: The sun and the moon They are two signs of God that do not cause anyone’s death or life to eclipse, but they are two signs of God. So when you see them, pray And give charity. (Bukhari 1044, Muslim 618)"
8389,"(8389) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The same, except that Ibn Numayr said: So say “Allahu Akbar” and supplicate. (Muslim 618)"
8390,"(8390) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Abd al-Malik told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The sun eclipsed on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day Ibrahim, son of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, and the people said: It just collapsed. The sun was due to the death of Abraham, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and led the people in prayer with six rak’ahs and four prostrations. He began and said “Allahu Akbar.” Then he recited and prolonged the recitation, then he bowed in the same way as he had stood, then he raised his head from bowing and recited a recitation without the first recitation, then He bowed in a manner similar to what he had stood, then raised his head from the bowing, so he recited one recitation without the second, then he bowed in a manner similar to what he had stood, then raised his head. From bowing, then he descended into prostration and prostrated two prostrations, then he stood up and bowed three more rak’ahs, none of which were rak’ahs except the one The one before it was longer than the one after it, and his bowing was similar to his prostration, then he delayed and the rows behind him continued until he came to The women, then he advanced and the people advanced with him until he stood in his place, and he departed when he departed and the sun was shining, and he said: Oh, her. People: Indeed, the sun and the moon are two of the signs of God. They do not become eclipsed due to the death of a human being. So if you see any of that, then pray until You will be saved. (Muslim 9. Abu Dawud 1172)"
8391,"(8391) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib ibn Malik, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, prayed two rak’ahs during a solar eclipse."
8392,"(8392) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus informed us, on the authority of Al-Hasan: that Ali prayed ten rak’ahs with four rak’ahs during the eclipse. Prostrations."
8393,"(8393) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Sulayman al-Ahwal, on the authority of Tawus: The sun eclipsed during the time of Ibn Abbas. He prayed two rak'ahs on Zamzam, with four prostrations in each rak'ah."
8394,"(8394) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: The sun or the moon was eclipsed. At the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Indeed, the sun and the moon are signs of God that will not be diminished by the death of any of them. People, if that is the case, then pray until you are cleared. (Bukhari 1040. An-Nasa’i 1847)"
8395,"(8395) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: They used to say: If that happens, then pray Like your prayers until you are saved."
8396,"(8396) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asma’, who said: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, continued for a long time until he was overcome by fainting. He said: She said: Then the Messenger of God left. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and you have been manifested. (Bukhari 86. Muslim 624)"
8397,"(8397) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: So-and-so and so-and-so narrated to me, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The eclipse of the sun and the moon are two of the signs of God, so when you see that, be terrified. Prayer (Bazzar 1371. Tabarani 1094)"
8398,"(8398) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Hayyan ibn Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, and he was one of the The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I used to shoot arrows in Medina during the lifetime of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when the sun eclipsed and I threw it away, I said: By God, we will look at what happened to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. During a solar eclipse, he said: So I came to him while he was standing in prayer, raising his hand. He said: So he began to glorify God, praise, and glorify God. And he would praise and pray until he was saddened by her. He said: Then when he was saddened by her, he said, he recited two surahs and prayed two rak’ahs. (Muslim 27 Abu Dawud 1188)"
8399,"(8399) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, saying: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, he said: Tha’labah bin narrated to me. Abbad Al-Abdi: One day he witnessed a sermon by Samurah ibn Jundub, and he mentioned in his sermon a hadith on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Samurah said: One day, I and a boy from the Ansar were throwing a target for us at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, until when the sun was as long as two or three spears in the eye of the observer from the horizon, it became black until it became bright. It was as if she was putting her to sleep, and one of us said to his friend: Go with us to the mosque, and by God, this sun will speak to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace among his nation. He said: So we went to the mosque, and behold, he was prominent and celebrating. He said: And the Messenger of God agreed with us. When he went out to the people, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he proceeded and led us in prayer like the longest he had ever performed a prayer with us. We did not listen to him. A voice, then he prostrated with us as he had prostrated with us for the longest time in prayer. We have never heard a voice from him. He said: Then he did it in the second rak’ah. For example, he said: The appearance of the sun coincided with his sitting in the second rak’ah, so he gave the salutation. (Abu Dawud 1177, An-Nasa’i 1869)"
8400,"(8400) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The verses are prayed in six rak’ahs with four prostrations."
8401,"(8401) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I saw Ibn Umar running to... The mosque is in an eclipse, and with it are its sandals."
8402,"(8402) Waki’ told us, he said: Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He prays two rak’ahs in the eclipse."
8403,"(8403) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair bin Tamim bin Hudhalam, he said: It was In Kufa there was darkness, so Hunay ibn Nuwayra came with a companion of his until they entered upon Tamim ibn Hudhalam, who was one of the companions of Abdullah, and they found him praying. He said: So he said to them: Go back to your homes and pray until we finish what you see. He was commanded to do that."
8404,"(8404) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: If you are terrified of the horizon of The horizons of the heavens, so rush to prayer."
8405,"(8405) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Uzza, who said: The people were frightened by the eclipse of the sun. Or the moon, or something, and Al-Sha’bi said: You should visit the mosque, for it is part of the Sunnah."
8406,"(8406) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He prays two rak’ahs in the eclipse."
8407,"(8407) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Ziyad: Concerning the eclipse prayer, he said: He gets up and recites And he bows, and when he says: God hears those who praise Him, he looks at the moon. If he has not prayed, he recites, then bows, then raises his head. So when he says: God hears those who praise Him, he looks at the moon, and if he has not prayed, he recites, then bows, then raises his head, then when he says: God hears whoever praises Him. He looks at the moon, and if it is there, he prostrates, then gets up and intercedes for it by bowing, and if he does not, then he does not prostrate. He will prostrate evermore until you are manifested, when he is manifested. Then, if there is an eclipse yet, he will not pray this prayer."
8408,"(8408) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ishaq bin Uthman al-Kalabi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ayyub al-Hijri, who said: The sun was eclipsed. In Basra, and Ibn Abbas was the ruler of it, so he stood up and led the people in prayer, and he recited and recited for a long time, then he bowed and bowed for a long time. Then he raised his head, then prostrated, then he did the same the second time. When he finished, he said: This is how the verses are prayed. He said: So I said: What did he recite in them? He said: By Al-Baqarah and the family of Imran."
8409,"(8409) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Shayban informed us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas: When the sun was eclipsed during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he was called. By praying together, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kneeled two rak’ahs during his prostration, then he got up and performed two rak’ahs during his prostration. He prostrated, then he was removed from the sun. He said: Aisha said: I have never prostrated or bowed as long as he was taller than him. (Bukhari 1045. Muslim 20)"
8410,"(8410) Mus’ab bin Al-Miqdam told us, he said: Zayed told us, he said: Ziyad bin Alaqih said: I heard Al-Mughirah bin Shu`ba says: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day Abraham died, so the people said: It eclipsed. Because of the death of Abraham, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Indeed, the sun and the moon are signs of God. They will not be eclipsed due to the death of Abraham. Uhud or his life, so when you see them, pray to God and pray until they are revealed. (Bukhari 6199. Ahmad 4/249)"
8411,"(8411) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zaid bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed in There are two rak'ahs for an eclipse, and he recites one of them with the star."
8412,"(8412) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Mujma’ told us, on the authority of Al-Majishun, he said: I heard Aban bin Uthman. He recited in Kusuf: {A questioner asked}"
8413,"(8413) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Abi led us in prayer. For the night when the moon was eclipsed, like our prayer in Ramadan, he said and recited the first thing he recited {Yasin and the Wise Qur’an}."
8414,"(8414) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to us during an earthquake that occurred. In Syria, go out on the Monday of such-and-such month. And whoever of you is able to give zakat, let him do so. For God Almighty said: {Successful has certainly been he who purifies himself and mentions the name of his Lord and prays}"
8415,"(8415) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais Al-Abdi, on the authority of Tha’labah bin Abbad, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer during an eclipse, but we did not hear his voice. (Tirmidhi 562, Nasa’i 1882)"
8416,"(8416) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Hanash Al-Kinani: that Ali spoke out loud in the Qur’anic verse. Eclipse"
8417,"(8417) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Ata’, he said: If the eclipse occurs after the afternoon And after dawn, they rose and mentioned their Lord, but they did not pray."
8418,"(8418) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If the sun eclipses at a time during which it is not permissible to pray He said: They call on you."
8419,"(8419) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, that Ibn Abbas led them in prayer during an earthquake that occurred for four days. Prostrations in which he bowed six times."
8420,"(8420) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shahr, who said: Medina was shaken during the reign of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Indeed, your Lord seeks your admonition, so admonish Him."
8421,"(8421) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiyy ibn Abi Ubaid, she said: The earth shook. On the promise of Omar until the curtains aligned and Abdullah bin Omar agreed to that while he was praying but did not turn around. She said: So Omar addressed the people He said: You told it, you have been hasty. She said: I do not know it except that he said: If she returns, I will be expelled from among your appearance."
8422,"(8422) Waki’, said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Kinanah, on the authority of his father, who said: One of the princes sent me to Ibn Abbas to ask him about rain? Ibn Abbas said: What prevented him from asking me? Then Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out, humble, humble, humble, supplicating, and praying, and he prayed two rak’ahs. As he prays on Eid, and he did not get engaged like you. (Tirmidhi 558, Abu Dawud 1160)"
8423,"(8423) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Harithah bin Mudarib al-Abdi, He said: We went out with Abu Musa to seek water, and he led us in two rak'ahs of prayer without the call to prayer or iqamah."
8424,"(8424) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: We went out with Abdullah bin Zayd. Al-Ansari asked us for water, so he prayed two rak'ahs, and Zaid bin Arqam succeeded him."
8425,"(8425) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hilal: He witnessed Omar bin Abdul Aziz starting to pray for rain. By praying before the sermon, he said: And I saw him draw water and he changed his robe."
8426,"(8426) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of his paternal uncle, He said: I witnessed the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, going out to draw water, facing the qiblah, turning his back to the people, and turning his cloak around He prayed two rak'ahs and recited the Qur'an out loud. (Bukhari 1025, Abu Dawud 1155)"
8427,"(8427) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, On the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to the prayer place to draw water. When he called, he faced the qiblah and turned around his robe. (Bukhari 1028, Muslim 611)"
8428,"(8428) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Issa bin Hafs bin Asim, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Marwan Al-Aslami, on the authority of his father, He said: We went out with Omar bin Al-Khattab to draw water, but he did nothing more than asking for forgiveness."
8429,"(8429) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: That Omar ibn Al-Khattab went out to draw water and went up. pulpit and said: {Ask forgiveness of your Lord. Indeed, He is ever Forgiving. He sends the heavens upon you in abundance and provides you with wealth and children. And He will make for you gardens and make for you rivers, {Ask forgiveness of your Lord, for He is Ever Forgiving} Then he descended and they said: O Prince For the believers, if I were to ask for something to drink, he said: I have asked for it by the glories of the heavens from which the drops descend."
8430,"(8430) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Aslam al-Ijli, who said: Some bitter people went out to seek rain, and Ibrahim went out. With them, when they had finished they stood up to pray, but Abraham returned and did not pray with them."
8431,"(8431) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He went out with Al-Mughirah bin Abdullah Al-Thaqafi. He asked for water, he said: So he prayed Al-Mughirah, and Abraham returned to where he saw him and prayed."
8432,"Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Baqi bin Mukhlid, may God have mercy on him, told us: Abu Bakr told us, he said:
(8432) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: Is prayer better? He said: The length of Qunoot. (Muslim 520, Ibn Majah 1421)"
8433,"(8433) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He was standing in prayer until his feet were wet, and he was told, and he said: Shall I not be a grateful servant?"
8434,"(8434) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, and Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Alaqah, on the authority of al-Mughirah ibn Shu`bah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is like him. (Bukhari 4836. Muslim 79)"
8435,"(8435) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A long standing period is more beloved to me than many things. Bowing and prostration."
8436,"(8436) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hajjaj bin Hassan told us, he said: I heard Abu Majliz, or I asked Abu A summary of the night prayer. Is the longest recitation more beloved to you, or a lot of bowing and prostrating? He said: No, but the length of the recitation."
8437,"(8437) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Yahya bin Rafi’, who said: It was said: Do not prolong Reciting during prayer, Satan will come to you and tempt you."
8438,"(8438) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, he said: He narrated to me that a man came to Abu Dharr said: Where is Abu Dharr? They said: He is at the foot of that mountain among his spoils. He said: So I came to him, and behold, he was praying, and behold, he was praying. Standing and doing a lot of bowing and prostration. He said: When he prayed, I said: O Abu Dhar, I saw you praying, standing less and bowing a lot. And prostration, and he said: It was narrated that no Muslim prostrated to God as deeply as he prostrated except that God raised him in rank and atoned for him. It is a sin"
8439,"(8439) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Mus’ab Al-Aslami; That a boy from Islam was serving the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he was relieved for him and said: O Messenger of God, pray to God that He will admit me to Paradise, or grant me your intercession. He said: Yes, and I mean abundant prostration. (Muslim 2260, Abu Dawud 1314)"
8440,"(8440) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin, on the authority of Masruq: He used to pray until His wife sits crying behind him."
8441,"(8441) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Mara’, who said: Abdullah said: As long as you are in Prayer knocks at the king’s door, and whoever knocks frequently at the king’s door is about to have it opened for him."
8442,"(8442) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Long standing during prayer is better than bowing and prostrating."
8443,"(8443) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythama, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Qays, who said: If you feel well, hasten it. And when Satan comes to you and says: You have been shown off, so increase her length."
8444,"(8444) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he eats or drinks during prayer, he faces the prayer."
8445,"(8445) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Aban Al-Attar, on the authority of Al-Salt bin Rashid, who said: Tawoos was asked about drinking during prayer? He said: No."
8446,"(8446) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Hajjaj and Ibrahim: They both hated it. Drinking during prayer"
8447,"(8447) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: It is not permissible to eat during prayer."
8448,"(8448) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: There is no harm in drinking while the imam is giving the Friday sermon."
8449,"(8449) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Al-Zubayr: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he sent Abdullah bin Unais to Khalid bin Sufyan, saying: When I approached him, and that was at the time of the afternoon, I was afraid that There would be no effort or practice, so I prayed while walking. (Abu Dawud 1243. Ahmad 3/496)"
8450,"(8450) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja`far, on the authority of Abu al-Saba’i, he said: I saw Mujahid He came from Al-Batha’i, and when he came to the Sacred Mosque, he recited his prostration and prostrated. I mentioned that to Ata’. He said: What a wonder That? The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were praying and walking."
8451,"(8451) Mukhlid bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: I asked him about the man. He prays while walking? He said: There is no problem if he nods."
8452,"(8452) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr. He said: If one of us prays while striving, meaning in war."
8453,"(8453) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Azraq ibn Qays, on the authority of Abu Barzah: That he prayed while holding on to his hands. His animal while he walked."
8454,"(8454) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Qadamiya Al-Amiri narrated to us, on the authority of Jisra Bint Dajjaja, on the authority of Abu Dharr: That the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He repeated these verses until the morning: {If You punish them, then they are Your servants, and if You forgive them, then You are You are the Mighty, the Wise. (Nasa’i 1083. Ahmad 5/170)"
8455,"(8455) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sa`id bin Ubaid al-Tai narrated to us, saying: I heard Sa`id bin Jubayr while he was praying. With them in the month of Ramadan, these verses are repeated: {So they will know when the shackles are around their necks and the chains are being dragged therein. boiling water, then they will be burned in the Fire}"
8456,"(8456) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, that Tamim al-Dari repeated This verse: {Or is it sufficient for those who committed evil deeds that We should make them like those who believed and did righteous deeds, whether He erased them? And their deaths}"
8457,"(8457) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ajlan, on the authority of Nasir Abi Tu’ma, the client of al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym, he said: Al-Rabi’ ibn Khuthaym was praying, so he passed by these verses: {Or is it sufficient for those who committed evil deeds?} until He sealed it and repeated it until the morning."
8458,"(8458) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Mu’awiyah bin Qurayh, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Mughaffal saying: During his journey in the year of the conquest, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited Surat Al-Fath on his camel, so he returned to its recitation. Muawiyah said: Were it not that I fear that people will gather against me, I would have told you what I read. (Bukhari 4281. Muslim 239)"
8459,"(8459) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: They loved to bring back verses from another person. The night"
8460,"(8460) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I see it on the authority of Abraham, he said: There is no harm for a man to stop at the verses. So he repeats it."
8461,"(8461) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah informed us, on the authority of Abraham, in the Almighty’s saying: {And when the Qur’an is recited, listen to it. And listen. He said: Concerning the written prayer."
8462,"(8462) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, we were told on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Concerning the Imam’s sermons on the Friday prayer."
8463,"(8463) Hushaym told us, he said: Juwaybir told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: In the prescribed prayer, and when dhikr."
8464,"(8464) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi. On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Mujahid. On the authority of Abu Al-Miqdam, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Quran, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Mughaffal: In the words of God Almighty: {And when the Qur’an is recited, listen To Him and be silent. They said: In prayer."
8465,"(8465) Hushaym told us, he said: We were told by someone who heard Al-Hasan say: At the prescribed prayer, and at the time of remembrance."
8466,"(8466) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Hijri, on the authority of Abu Iyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: They were They talk about the prayer, so the verse was revealed: {And when the Qur’an is recited, listen to it and be silent.} They said: This is about the prayer."
8467,"(8467) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite And a man was reciting, and it was revealed: {And when the Qur’an is recited, listen to it and be silent}"
8468,"(8468) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I heard Ibrahim bin Abi Hurr, that he heard Mujahid say In these verses: {And when the Qur’an is recited, listen to it and be silent.} He said: in prayer and sermons on the day of Friday prayers."
8469,"(8469) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: {And when the Qur’an is recited, listen to it and be silent.} He said: In the written prayer."
8470,"(8470) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the nosebleeds do not subside, he will be distressed, then he hasten to pray."
8471,"(8471) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: If The shaking did not stop, and his companion nodded."
8472,"(8472) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’: About a man who felt compassion and did not refrain from it until he feared missing out. Prayer. He said: He clamps his nostrils with a cloth and hastens to pray. I said: Then it falls into his stomach. He said: Even if."
8473,"(8473) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He will manage what is between him and that he will fear the end of time. If that is the case, start praying, meaning nosebleed."
8474,"(8474) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Al-Miswar Ibn Makramah: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab prayed and his wound would bleed."
8475,"(8475) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: The superiority of a man’s prayer in congregation over his prayer alone is twenty-few degrees. (Ahmad 1/376, Bazzar 458)"
8476,"(8476) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hilal ibn Maimun, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yazid al-Laythi, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A man’s prayer in congregation is five times greater than his prayer alone. And twenty degrees, and if he prays in a land that is deserted and completes its ablution, bowing, and prostration, his prayer will amount to fifty. To a degree (Abu Dawud 561, Ibn Majah 788)"
8477,"(8477) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Praying in congregation is superior to the prayer of one man alone by twenty-five degrees. (Bukhari 648 and Muslim 245)"
8478,"(8478) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubad Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: A man’s prayer in congregation is twenty-seven times superior to his prayer alone. (Muslim 451, Ibn Majah 789)"
8479,"(8479) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Praying in congregation is twenty-five times greater than praying alone. (Bukhari 648 and Muslim 450)"
8480,"(8480) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The virtue of prayer The congregational prayer is twenty-four times greater than the prayer of a man alone."
8481,"(8481) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Double Congregational prayer is twenty-five times greater than the single prayer."
8482,"(8482) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: Abdullah said: A man’s prayer in... Praying in congregation is twenty-some times better than praying in the market or alone. He said: He was commanded to pray closely together. Sins"
8483,"(8483) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, who said: We entered upon Zaid bin Thabit, and he He prays on a mat and prostrates on it, and he said: The superiority of congregational prayer over solo prayer is twenty-five degrees."
8484,"(8484) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Praying with the imam is superior to praying alone. Twenty-seven degrees."
8485,"(8485) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The virtue of prayer The congregation is twenty-five times greater than the number of people in the mosque, and if they are more, then it is equal to the number of people in the mosque. A man said: And if they were ten thousand? He said: Yes, even if they are forty thousand."
8486,"(8486) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqiyya, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: On the number of people in the mosque."
8487,"(8487) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Kathir ibn Aflah, who said: We were in Medina in Abu Yusuf went to reckon with us, we will reckon with him, and with us was Zayd bin Thabit, and he said: A man’s prayer with the imam is doubled over his prayer alone. Twenty-five degrees."
8488,"(8488) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: Abdullah said: A man’s prayer increases his A congregational prayer for a single prayer is twenty-four degrees, or twenty-five degrees."
8489,"(8489) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Beware of the shirk of secrets. They said: What is the shirk of secrets? He said: If one of you stands up and embellishes his prayer with effort so that people will look at him, that is the polytheism of secrets. (Bayhaqi 290. Ahmad 5/429)"
8490,"(8490) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Whoever prays a prayer while the people If they see it, let him pray if there is something like it alone. Otherwise, it is only an act of disdain by which he disdains his Lord."
8491,"(8491) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Hudhayfy, a similar story."
8492,"(8492) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Musa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, prays in the garment in which he has intercourse. (Ahmed 217)"
8493,"(8493) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, who said: A man asked Jabir bin Samurah if I should pray in a garment. And I agree with it? He said: If anything happens to it, wash it, but if nothing happens to it, there is no harm in praying in it."
8494,"(8494) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Bashir, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: This is so that you may know that we agree about it. And we pray in it."
8495,"(8495) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: He was asked about the garment in which one has intercourse. Should he pray in it? He said: I said: Yes, I said: Should we sprinkle it with water? He said: Nothing increases it except it stinks."
8496,"(8496) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, he said: Damra bin Habib narrated to me, he said: Muhammad bin Salih narrated to me. Abu Sufyan Al-Thaqafi, that the mother of his beloved, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, praying in a garment. Ali and Ali were in it as long as they were. (Bukhari 2888, Ahmad 6/325)"
8497,"(8497) Shababi told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Suwayd bin Qays, on the authority of Mu’awiyah bin Hadij, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan: He asked the mother of his beloved son Abi Sufyan whether the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, prays in the garment in which he used to have intercourse with her? She said: Yes, as long as he does not see any harm in it. (Abu Dawud 369. Ahmad 6/427)"
8498,"(8498) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a short man who was said to be To him: He prostrated and said: Praise be to God who did not make me like this. (Abu Dawud 2768. Tirmidhi 1578)"
8499,"(8499) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awn Al-Thaqafi Muhammad bin Ubaidullah, on the authority of a man he did not name, When Abu Bakr opened the dove, he prostrated."
8500,"(8500) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awn al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Yahya bin al-Jazzar: that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. A man passed by him some time ago and prostrated, as did Abu Bakr and Omar."
8501,"(8501) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father: that Omar came to him He opened from the front of the dove and prostrated."
8502,"(8502) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais al-Hamdani, on the authority of a sheikh of theirs who was called Abu Musa said: I bore witness to Ali when the Mukhdraj was brought to him, he prostrated."
8503,"(8503) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Abu Musa: When Ali was brought with the Mukhdaj, he prostrated."
8504,"(8504) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: He disliked the prostration of gratitude. Mansour said: And it reached me that Abu Bakr and Omar prostrated with gratitude."
8505,"(8505) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by A Benghashi man prostrated and said: Ask God for well-being."
8506,"(8506) Hushaym told us, he said: Al-Kalbi told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When the marriage Zainab Zayd ibn Harithah set off until he asked permission to come to Zainab. He said: Then Zainab said: What do I have to do with Zayd? He said: So he sent To her, and he said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to you. He said: So she gave him permission, so he gave her good news that God had He married her to his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So she fell down, prostrating to God in thanks. (Ibn Saad 102)"
8507,"(8507) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham: He used to hate his prostration of joy, And he says: There is neither bowing nor prostration in it."
8508,"(8508) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Suwayd bin Ubaid al-Ijli narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Mumin al-Wathili, who said: I bore witness to Ali. When the Mukhdraj was brought, he prostrated."
8509,"(8509) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The prostration of gratitude is a supplication."
8510,"(8510) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail bin Zarbiyy told us, he said: Raban bin Sabriya al-Hanafi told us: He witnessed the day of Nahrawan. He said: I was among those who took out the mammal and announced it to the Most High before it came to God. So we came to him and he was prostrating and rejoicing in him."
8511,"(8511) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Sa’sa’, On the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abdul Rahman bin Awf, he said: I went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him while he was prostrating. When he left, I said: I prostrated for a long time. He said: I prostrated in thanks to my Lord for what He has bestowed upon me among my nation. (Ahmad 1/191, Abu Ali 843)"
8512,"(8512) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, received his sight. May God bless him and grant him peace while he was praying with his two fingers. He said: So he said to him: O Saad, one of the other. (Tirmidhi 3557, Abu Dawud 1494)"
8513,"(8513) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: He saw a man He called with both his fingers, but he finished it, and said, with one finger, the right."
8514,"(8514) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rashid Abi Saad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, he said: It was When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat in prayer, he placed his hand on his thigh and pointed with his finger in supplication. (Muslim 408 and Abu Dawud 979)"
8515,"(8515) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Tamimi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is sincerity, It means supplication with the finger."
8516,"(8516) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abi Yahya, he said: They were the companions of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, leading one of them to another, meaning pointing with the finger in supplication."
8517,"(8517) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, that he said: The supplications are like this and indicated With one finger Satan oppresses you."
8518,"(8518) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Alqamiya, on the authority of Aisha, she said: God loves to be called upon. Thus, she pointed with one finger."
8519,"(8519) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Salama ibn Alqamiya, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Kathir ibn Aflah, who said: I prayed, and when he was at the end of the Qa’dah, I said thus and so, and Ibn Aliyah pointed with his finger, and Ibn Umar took this. It means the left side."
8520,"(8520) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He used to wave his finger during prayer."
8521,"(8521) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Khaythamiya: He used to hold fifty-three meetings, and he would sign With his finger"
8522,"(8522) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Whenever they saw a person praying with his two fingers They struck one of them and said: There is only one God."
8523,"(8523) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man points with his finger during prayer, then it is good and it is good. Monotheism, but he does not point with his two fingers, for it is disliked."
8524,"(8524) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah: That his father used to wave his finger during supplications, but he did not He moves it."
8525,"(8525) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ma’abad ibn Khalid, on the authority of Qais ibn Sa’d, who said: There was no more than that. And he pointed with his finger."
8526,"(8526) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Asim ibn Qadamah, on the authority of Malik ibn Numayr al-Khuza’i, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting during prayer, placing his right hand on his thigh and pointing with his finger. (Abu Dawud 983. Ibn Hibban 1946)"
8527,"(8527) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw Sa’d praying With his two fingers, he said: “One, one.”"
8528,"(8528) Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Aamir bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God When God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sits and makes supplication, he places his right hand on his right thigh, and his left hand on His left thigh, and he pointed with his index finger, and placed his thumb on his middle finger, and touched his palm. His left knee.
(Muslim 1131, Abu Dawud 980)"
8529,"(8529) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajar, he said: I saw the Prophet praying. May God bless him and grant him peace, placing the edge of his right elbow on his right thigh, circling his thumb and middle finger, and raising the next finger. The thumb supplicates with it. (Abu Dawud 726. Ahmad 4/319)"
8530,"(8530) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Amr bin Al-Ahwas, who said: Abu Hilal told me, on the authority of Abu Barza: that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for two men and raised his hand. (Abu Ali 7440)"
8531,"(8531) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Hayyan bin Umair, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Samurah: That the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, he raised his hand, meaning in supplication."
8532,"(8532) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah, on the authority of Ibn Abu Dhabab, on the authority of Saul bin Saad, said: I have never seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spreading his hand in supplications over A pulpit or anything else, and I saw his hands as high as his shoulders and he was praying. (Abu Dawud 1098. Ahmad 5/337)"
8533,"(8533) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was not He raises his hands in any supplication except when praying for rain. (Bukhari 1031, Abu Dawud 1163)"
8534,"(8534) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim bin Tarfi, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us and said: Why do I see you raising your hands as if they were tails? Horses of the sun, be still in prayer. (Muslim 1198, Abu Dawud 909)"
8535,"(8535) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: He was asked: Was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Does he raise his hand? He said: Yes. The people complained to him during the gathering and said: O Messenger of God, the rain has failed, the land is barren, and wealth has perished. He said: So he raised He prayed until I saw the whites of his armpits. (Bukhari 612, Muslim 612)"
8536,"(8536) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: Do not stand up and pray as What the Jews do in their churches."
8537,"(8537) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Ibn al-Asbaaniy, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman: He saw a man calling He stood up after he left and insulted him or insulted him."
8538,"(8538) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdah ibn Abi Lubab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he hated it."
8539,"(8539) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Two things: What is innovation is for a man to stand up facing the direction of prayer after he has finished praying and to perform the prostration. Secondly, he believes that it is his right to stick his buttocks to the ground before he gets up."
8540,"(8540) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he used to hate standing up after her because he looked like her. With the Jews"
8541,"(8541) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I said to Al-Mughirah: When Abraham left, he was reluctant to stand up. Does the person facing the qiblah raise his hand? He said: Yes."
8542,"(8542) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Abdullah: It has reached him that a people remember Allah He stood up and came to them and said: What is this terrible thing? They said: We heard God saying: {So remember God standing and sitting, and on your sides}, and He said: This is only if the man is not able He prays standing, he prays sitting."
8543,"(8543) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Jamil bin Zaid, who said: I saw Ibn Umar entering the house and praying two rak’ahs, then He turned and prayed two rak'ahs following the Rukn, then I went out and left him standing, supplicating and saying ""Allahu Akbar."""
8544,"(8544) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: I saw Al-Hasan raising his gaze to the heavens in prayer, supplicating while he was Standing"
8545,"(8545) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Mujahid: He heard a man raising his voice in supplication, He stoned him with pebbles."
8546,"(8546) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: O people, you do not Do you call upon a deaf person or an absent person? This means raising one’s voice during supplication."
8547,"(8547) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Yazid bin Aban, on the authority of Anas. On the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan: They both disliked the man sitting with him hearing any of the supplications."
8548,"(8548) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They used to strive hard in supplications, and you would not hear anything except a whisper."
8549,"(8549) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Sadiqah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. He said: When the praying person prays, he talks to his Lord, so let each one of you know what he is talking to, and do not rebel against each other. Some (Ahmad 2/67 Bazzar 726)"
8550,"(8550) Ibn Fudail and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: We were with The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on a journey, and the people started shouting “Allahu Akbar” loudly, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: O people, be kind to yourselves. You are not calling on a deaf person, nor on someone who is absent. You are calling on a Hearer who is near and he is with you. (Bukhari 2992 and Abu Dawud 1523)"
8551,"(8551) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naseeb, who said: I prayed next to Saeed bin Al-Musayyab in Morocco. When I sat in the second rak’ah, I raised my voice in supplication and he cursed me. When I left, I said to him: What did you dislike from me? He said: You thought that God was not close to you?"
8552,"(8552) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu Iyas, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The supplications between the call to prayer and the iqamah are not rejected. (Tirmidhi 212. Ahmad 3/119)"
8553,"(8553) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Abu Marara, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The best of hours The times for prayers, so pray within them."
8554,"(8554) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It was desirable Supplications at the Maghrib call to prayer, and he said: It is an hour in which supplications are answered."
8555,"(8555) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ziyad bin Anam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Amr said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If the imam sits and then speaks, his prayer has been completed, and whoever was behind him has Of those who performed the prayer with him like that. (Tirmidhi 408 and Abu Dawud 617)"
8556,"(8556) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If the imam sits on the fourth Then he spoke, and his prayer was complete, so let him stand wherever he wants."
8557,"(8557) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Kufi, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of Ali, who said: When he trembled during his prayer After the last prostration, his prayer has been completed."
8558,"(8558) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab and al-Hasan, who said: When he raises his head, then he spoke, and his prayer was sufficient for him."
8559,"(8559) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he raises his head from prostration, his prayer has ended."
8560,"(8560) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: If he sat after completing the prayer, then he broke the fast before he He says the tashahhud or after the tashahhud before the imam says the salaam. It is permissible, so let him leave."
8561,"(8561) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talhah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he completed bowing and prostration, then he did it, then he His prayer is over, even if he does not recite the Tashahid."
8562,"(8562) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he sat down after he had finished the last prostration, let him leave. Let him perform ablution, and when he comes back, let him pray the shahada as long as he does not speak. If he speaks, he will resume the prayer."
8563,"(8563) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, about a gift like that."
8564,"(8564) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he used to say: Until he greets you."
8565,"(8565) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ma’qil, on the authority of Ata’: Concerning a man, he said: When he said: Peace be upon us and upon the servants of God. The righteous are rewarded."
8566,"(8566) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: Until he recites the tashahhud, or sits for an amount of time. Al-Shahed"
8567,"(8567) Mu’tamar told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; Concerning a man reciting the tashahid and then speaking, he said: This has completed his prayer."
8568,"(8568) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Do you know a prayer that is performed while sitting? What about it all? He said: This is a man who performed a rak'ah from the Maghrib prayer and sat in it all of them."
8569,"(8569) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Masruq and Jundub came to you in prayer from the west, so when The imam said the salutation, Masruq stood up and added a rak’ah to it, then he sat down and Jundub stood up for them all, then he sat down at the end of it and mentioned that. To Abdullah, he said: Both of them did well, and I will do as Masruq did, which is more beloved to me."
8570,"(8570) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim: That a grasshopper and Masruq went out wanting to pray. Maghrib, so they performed a rak'ah with the imam. When the imam said the salaam, Masruq sat in the second rak'ah, and Jundub did not sit. He said and recited Jundub in the rak’ah that he joined but did not recite Masruq, so they went to Ibn Masoud and mentioned to him what they had done, so Abdullah said: Both of you did well, and I do what Masruq did."
8571,"(8571) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yahya, he said: Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Janni narrated to us, on the authority of Saad said: When he performs one of the four rak’ahs with the imam, he should not sit except in the last of them. You sat down"
8572,"(8572) Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man performing a rak’ah from the west. He said: He sits in All of us"
8573,"(8573) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Labid, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, I said: Tell me about The prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: His night prayers in Ramadan and elsewhere were thirteen rak’ahs, including two dawn rak’ahs. (Tirmidhi 439. Abu Dawud 1335)"
8574,"(8574) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Abu Jamra, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said, I heard him say: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he prays thirteen rak’ahs during the night. (Bukhari 1138, Muslim 194)"
8575,"(8575) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sharhabeel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We came with the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him from Al-Hudaybiyah, even when we were among the companions. Mu’adh said: Who will give us water in our watering cans? He said: So I went out with some young men with me until we came to the girls, so we gave them water to drink and drew water for, and when it was after the dark of the night, then, A man was disputing with his camel. He said: Then, behold, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I took his camel and lowered it, and he came forward. He prayed the evening prayer while I was on his right, then he prayed thirteen rak’ahs. (Ahmad 3/380, Abu Ali 2213)"
8576,"(8576) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Abu Rishdin Kurayb Mawla of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: You spent the night with your aunt Maimunah, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spent the night. Then I saw him getting up during the night and praying either eleven rak’ahs or thirteen rak’ahs (Bukhari 6316. Muslim 181)"
8577,"(8577) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray nine rak’ahs at night. (Tirmidhi 443. Ahmad 6/253)"
8578,"(8578) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Omar prayed a prayer at the House and recited {for the thousands of Quraysh} So he started gesturing to the House and saying: {So let them worship the Lord of this House, who has fed them against hunger and made them safe from fear}."
8579,"(8579) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aws, who said: My grandfather was Aws sometimes. He prays and points to me while he is praying, so I give him his sandals."
8580,"(8580) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Hisham, who said: My father used to meow during prayer. He said: Aisha used to do that."
8581,"(8581) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in gesturing during prayer."
8582,"(8582) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, who said: I was struck by a nosebleed while I was circumambulating the Kaaba, and I passed a peacock who was praying, so he pointed. Until I wash it with water, then come back."
8583,"(8583) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad may have gestured with his hand while praying."
8584,"(8584) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I said to Ibrahim: Does a man point to something during prayer? He said: There is busyness in prayer."
8585,"(8585) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: He did not see any harm in a man gesticulating during prayer."
8586,"(8586) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I told him: You will fulfill the need while I am in prayer. So I motioned to the maid with my hands and said: We will do that."
8587,"(8587) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I saw Amr ibn Maymun praying, so he gestured to A man with his hand."
8588,"(8588) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was struck by epilepsy. On the authority of his horse, it fell on the trunk of a palm tree and its foot broke off, so we went in to visit him while he was praying in a drinking place. Aisha was sitting and we prayed with his prayer while we were standing, then we entered upon him another time while he was praying sitting and we prayed. With his prayer while we were standing, he motioned to us to sit down."
8589,"(8589) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained. May God bless him and grant him peace. Some of his companions entered and visited him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed while sitting. They prayed. He stood up for his prayer and motioned to them to sit down, so they sat down."
8590,"(8590) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim: He was asked about gesturing in Prayer? He said: There is busyness in prayer."
8591,"(8591) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abdullah bin Suraqi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abd. God, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying on his camel towards the east during the Anmar battle. (Bukhari 4140. Ahmad 3/300)"
8592,"(8592) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. On the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He used to pray for His mount was voluntary when traveling wherever it headed and he nodded, prostrating lower than bowing. (Muslim 32)"
8593,"(8593) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya bin Amara al-Mazini, on the authority of Sa`id bin Yasar On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, praying on a donkey towards the east, while heading towards... Khaybara (Muslim 487. Abu Dawud 1219)"
8594,"(8594) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent me. He greeted Hajj and said: I came to him while he was praying on his camel towards the east, and the prostration was lower than the bowing. (Tirmidhi 351, Abu Dawud 1220)"
8595,"(8595) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to pray on his camel while traveling wherever it took it. (Malik 26)"
8596,"(8596) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: Ali used to pray. On his mount wherever it is headed, and he performs prostration rather than bowing."
8597,"(8597) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman: that Abu Dharr used to pray on his camel while he was Before the east, he was shaking his head, and it was said to him: Were you asleep? He said: No, but I was praying."
8598,"(8598) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Jabir, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray on his mount towards the east, so if he wanted to He prayed the obligatory prayer. He descended and faced the qiblah. (Bukhari 1099. Muslim 383)"
8599,"(8599) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Al-Jaroud bin Abi Sabra Al-Tamimi, who said: Amr bin Al-Tamimi narrated to me. Abi Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Jaroud bin Abi Sabra, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He wanted to voluntarily pray on his mount, so he faced the qiblah and said “Allahu Akbar” for the prayer, then he prayed on his mount and prayed wherever they were. She was crowned with it. (Abu Dawud 1218, Darqutni 395)"
8600,"(8600) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to pray over his camel wherever it headed, and Ibn Umar used to do that. (Muslim 4868 Tirmidhi 2958)"
8601,"(8601) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Al-Harith Al-Taifi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Burda bin Abi Musa, on the authority of his father: He used to pray on his camel wherever it took him during the journey."
8602,"(8602) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Atiq, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa: He used to pray on his camel while traveling wherever it took him."
8603,"(8603) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, who said: I saw a man praying on a gesticulating donkey. Without kissing."
8604,"(8604) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Shayba bin Qariz narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Bahi, the client of the Al-Zubayr family, who said: I accompanied Abdullah bin Omar from Mecca to Medina, and he was praying on his camel to the opposite direction."
8605,"(8605) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I accompanied Ibn Umar from Medina to Mecca. So he used to pray on his animal wherever it was facing him, so when it was the obligatory prayer he would come down and pray."
8606,"(8606) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad: that Abu Ayyub used to pray on his camel where She was crowned with it."
8607,"(8607) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Zayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan or others. There is no doubt about me: that the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. They used to pray on their animals wherever their faces were during their journeys."
8608,"(8608) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to pray on their camels and their animals wherever they were. Their faces were bare except for the obligatory prayer and the Witr prayer, for they used to connect them to the ground."
8609,"(8609) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Al-Qasim bin Muhammad: Should a man pray on his camel? He said: Yes, I said: Does he pray wherever his face is? He said: Yes, I said: Does it make prostration lower than bowing? He said: Yes."
8610,"(8610) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidi, who said: A man prays on his camel. Wherever his face was, then when the obligatory prayer was fulfilled, he descended."
8611,"(8611) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali: That his father Ali bin Hussein was praying on his camel while traveling wherever it headed."
8612,"(8612) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray on his camel while traveling, wherever it headed."
8613,"(8613) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Hazzaz: I asked Al-Dahhak about praying on an animal? He said: Where his face was, prostration was lower than bowing."
8614,"(8614) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran ibn Muslim, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafla, who said: We used to pray for Our beasts of war wherever we went."
8615,"(8615) Abdul-A’la narrated to us, or I narrated on his authority, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah. On the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray on his camel wherever it headed (Bukhari 1097. Muslim 40)"
8616,"(8616) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: I did not care, I prayed in The Hijr or in the Kaaba."
8617,"(8617) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I don’t care. I prayed in quarantine or at home."
8618,"(8618) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, he said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr, when he completed his tawaf, he entered the Hijr. So he prayed in it, and I saw Ali bin Hussein doing that."
8619,"(8619) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Al-Haytham, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: Al-Hijr is from The Kaaba"
8620,"(8620) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of Yahya bin Qamtiya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar: He said in these verses (So We will surely give you a kiss that will please you) He said: Abraham’s kiss under the gutter, meaning In the stone."
8621,"(8621) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Shayban informed us, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi Al-Sha’ath’i, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Yazid, on the authority of Aisha: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the stone, and he said: It is from the House. (Bukhari 7243. Muslim 405)"
8622,"(8622) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who goes to the people and they Sitting and saying “Allahu Akbar” then sitting? They said: When he stands, he will perform the iddah with that takbeer."
8623,"(8623) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud: He disliked reciting tithes in the Qur’an."
8624,"(8624) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It was disliked to pay tithing in the Qur’an, and that Something else is written in it."
8625,"(8625) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, similar to this."
8626,"(8626) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: He hated being written. In the Qur’an there is a tenor or a breakdown, and He says: Surah Al-Baqarah, and He says: The Surah in which Al-Baqarah is mentioned."
8627,"(8627) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’: He used to dislike tithing in the Qur’an, or writing it down. There is something in it other than that."
8628,"(8628) Abdah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, he said: I said to Abu Razin: I have a Qur’an that I want to seal. With gold and write at the beginning of every surah such-and-such verse. Abu Razin said: Do not add to it anything of this world. Say, Or a lot."
8629,"(8629) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad: He used to hate the conquests and the first days that There is a qāf and a kaaf in it."
8630,"(8630) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Sheikh, on the authority of Abdullah: He saw a mistake in the Qur’an, so he rubbed it and said: Do not mix it with anything else."
8631,"(8631) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham: He disliked tithing in the Qur’an."
8632,"(8632) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: He disliked tithing in the Qur’an."
8633,"(8633) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He disliked the dots and the end of a surah. Such and such"
8634,"(8634) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ara’, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: Strip the Qur’an, and do not mix with it what is not part of it."
8635,"(8635) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: Strip the Qur’an."
8636,"(8636) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It used to be said: Strip the Qur’an."
8637,"(8637) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, he said: Abdullah said: Strip the Qur’an."
8638,"(8638) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: I said to Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad: What prevented you from being Did you ask as Abraham asked? He said: It used to be said: They stripped the Qur’an."
8639,"(8639) Malik and Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Habhab: that Abu Al-Aliyah was He disliked the sentences that were written in the Qur’an, opening and closing, and he said: Strip the Qur’an."
8640,"(8640) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali: He hated to The Qur’an is written in small copies of the Qur’an."
8641,"(8641) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was said: Magnify the Qur’an. That means, enlarge the Qur’an."
8642,"(8642) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hakimah al-Abdi, who said: We used to write the Qur’an. With the Kufa, then Ali passes by us and gets up and looks and is impressed by our handwriting and says: Thus, enlighten what God has enlightened."
8643,"(8643) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Shaddad al-Azdi narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Sulaiman al-Abdi, on the authority of Abu Hakimah Al-Abdi said: We used to write the Qur’an in Kufa, and Ali would pass by us while we were writing, and he would say: Yes. Your pen, he said: So I cut out some of it and then wrote, and he said: Thus, enlighten what God Almighty has enlightened."
8644,"(8644) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali: He disliked that the Qur’an be written in The small Qur’an."
8645,"(8645) Waki’ and Ubaidullah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: He hated to say Mushaf."
8646,"(8646) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Continue looking at the Qur’an."
8647,"(8647) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: You came to him. While he was reading from the Qur’an, he said: This is my party with which I want to spend the night."
8648,"(8648) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythami, who said: I entered upon Abdullah bin Amr While he was reading from the Qur’an, he said: This is my party with which I want to spend the night."
8649,"(8649) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: The characteristic of the ancients was to look at the Qur’an. He said: Al-Ahnaf ibn Qays was When he left, he looked at the Qur’an."
8650,"(8650) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Shammisa Umm Salamah, on the authority of Aisha: She used to recite in The Qur’an, so when she passed the prostration, she stood up and prostrated."
8651,"(8651) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Sariya al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaim narrated to me, saying: If it is spring To read from the Qur’an, and if someone enters it, he covers him."
8652,"(8652) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, saying: I entered upon Abraham while he was reading from the Qur’an, so he asked for permission. A man came over it and covered it and said: This man does not see that I read about it every hour."
8653,"(8653) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They entered upon Uthman with the Qur’an in his lap."
8654,"(8654) Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Hilal told us, he said: Abu Salih Al-Uqaili told us, he said: Abu Al-Alaa Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir reads from the Qur’an until he faints."
8655,"(8655) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, who said: I saw Talha reading from the Qur’an."
8656,"(8656) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Familiarize yourself with these Mushafs. He is more detailed in blessings than the breasts of men, so let none of you say, “I forgot the verse. I have so much and so much,” said the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Rather, he forgot. (Muslim 229. An-Nasa’i 10561)"
8657,"(8657) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Familiarize yourself with the Qur’an, for by the one in whose hand my soul is, it is more detailed than the hearts of men. Of camels, of their calves. (Bukhari 5033 and Muslim 545)"
8658,"(8658) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The example of the Qur’an is that of a camel that has been hampered. If its owner mounts it, it catches it, but if it abandons it, it goes away. (Muslim 227 Ahmad 2/36)"
8659,"(8659) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I will read my party, or My party led me while I was lying on my bed."
8660,"(8660) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ali, who said: I heard my father saying: I heard Uqba ibn Amir saying: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Learn the Qur’an and recite it, for by the One in whose hand my soul is, it is quicker in its explanation than Men's hearts are as blessed as their minds. (Ahmad 4/1461 Tabarani 802)"
8661,"(8661) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zayd bin Abdullah bin al-Shakhir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever recites the Qur’an in less than three times will not understand it. (Tirmidhi 2949. Abu Dawud 1389)"
8662,"(8662) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar and Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Badhimah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: He said: Abdullah: Whoever recites the Qur’an in less than three times, then he has failed."
8663,"(8663) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba. He said: Ibn Masoud used to recite the Qur’an every three days, and he rarely sought help during the day."
8664,"(8664) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu: He used to complete the Qur’an. In the eighth"
8665,"(8665) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Abu Qalabab: That he used to complete the Qur’an in eight, and that Tamim al-Dari was The Qur’an concludes with seven chapters."
8666,"(8666) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: Muadh used to hate it. The Qur’an is recited in less than three days."
8667,"(8667) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The lion was reciting the Qur’an during the month of Ramadan. For two nights, he concluded it in six days, unlike Ramadan, and Alqamiya used to complete it in five days."
8668,"(8668) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya: He used to recite The Qur’an is recited in five, and Al-Aswad bin Yazid used to recite it in six."
8669,"(8669) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd used to recite the Qur’an. In every seventh, and Alqamah and Al-Aswad used to recite the one in five and the other in six, and Ibrahim used to read in In seven"
8670,"(8670) Abdullah bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: Urwah used to recite the Qur’an every seven days."
8671,"(8671) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: He used to lead the neighborhood in prayer in Ramadan, and he used to It concludes with seven."
8672,"(8672) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Ya’la al-Taifi narrated to us, on the authority of Othman bin Abdullah bin Aws Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of his grandfather Aws bin Hudhayfy, who said: A delegation from Thaqif came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: So We sent down in his dome, and our brothers sent down the oaths against Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He would come to us after dinner and speak to us, and the Quraysh were most suspicious of his speech, and he would say: We are not alike. In Mecca, they were oppressed and oppressed, and when we came to Medina, the war was a dispute between us and ours.
 He said: Then he made a longer night for us, and it became longer, so we said: O Messenger of God, you made a longer night for us. He said: A party of The Qur’an. I thought I would go out until I had finished it, so we asked the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, how the Messenger of God was. Does God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recite the Qur’an? He said: His party was three, five, seven, nine, eleven, and thirteen, and the Mufassal party. (Ahmad 4/343, Ibn Majah 1345)"
8673,"(8673) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Sa’id Al-Ansari, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father On the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, he said: Because I recite the Qur’an in a month that is more beloved to me than reciting it in the fifteenth, and because That I read it on fifteen days is more beloved to me than that I read it on ten days, and that I read it on ten days is more beloved to me than that I read it on ten days. At seven days I stand and pray."
8674,"(8674) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: Abdullah said: Read the Qur’an in Seven and do not recite it in three."
8675,"(8675) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, who said: He used to complete the Qur’an in every verse. Three days, then the day on which he concludes his fast becomes morning."
8676,"(8676) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, who said: A man came to Masruq and said: What do you say about a man who recites? The Qur’an in its entirety? Masruq said: It would be good if you took a Qur’an every Friday and put it in a house, you would almost fill it."
8677,"(8677) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: that Tamim al-Dari recited the entire Qur’an in one raka’."
8678,"(8678) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman, He said: I stood behind the shrine and prayed, and I wanted no one to overpower me that night, when a man appeared behind me. He winked at me and I did not turn to him. Then he winked at me and I turned around, and behold, it was Uthman bin Affan. I stepped aside and he came forward and recited the Qur’an. He performed one rak'ah, then left."
8679,"(8679) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Abi Sulaiman, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr saying: I recited the Qur’an in the Kaaba in one rak’ah."
8680,"(8680) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Uthman: He recited the Qur’an in a rak’ah in prayer. Layla"
8681,"(8681) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah: that he recited it in A night in Mecca."
8682,"(8682) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah and something similar."
8683,"(8683) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a companion of his, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I recited the Qur’an in the Ka’bah in Two rak'ahs"
8684,"(8684) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ali Al-Azdi used to complete the Qur’an. In Ramadan every night."
8685,"(8685) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Shutair ibn Shikal, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him on the Day of Ahzab: They distracted us from the middle prayer, the afternoon prayer. May God fill their homes and graves. Fire, then he prayed the Isha prayer between Maghrib and Isha. (Muslim 2051, Ahmad 1/81)"
8686,"(8686) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Ali: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, was fulfilling the obligation of the ditch, and he said: They distracted us from the middle prayer, the afternoon prayer until the sun set. God filled their houses, their graves, their bellies, and their insides with fire. (Muslim 204. Ahmad 1/152)"
8687,"(8687) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The middle prayer. Asr prayer"
8688,"(8688) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, he said: A man told me, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah: that Hafs The Mother of the Believers, she said: The middle prayer is the afternoon prayer {And stand before God in obedience}"
8689,"(8689) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Qais, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Umm Salama: She wrote a Qur’an. When she reached {Guard the prayers and the middle prayer}, she said: Write the afternoon prayer."
8690,"(8690) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Salih, he said: Musa ibn Zayd informed me, he said: I asked Abu Imam told him about the middle prayer, and he said: I do not think it is anything but dawn."
8691,"(8691) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of al-Zabarqan, on the authority of Zuhra, he said: We were sitting in The mosque was with Zayd bin Thabit. He was asked about the middle prayer and he said: It is the dhahr prayer. Then Usama passed by and he was asked about it and he said: It is the zuhr prayer. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to lead her in prayer with a stone. (Nasa’i 356. Ahmad 5/206)"
8692,"(8692) Hushaym told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: This is the Fajr prayer."
8693,"(8693) Hushaym told us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jaafar informed us, on the authority of someone who told him on the authority of Manzoor ibn Abi Tha’labah,"
8694,"(8694) Hushaym told us, he said: The common people told us, on the authority of Al-Ansari, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit: He used to say That"
8695,"(8695) Waki’ told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The middle prayer is a prayer. The afternoon"
8696,"(8696) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talhah, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Murr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: This is the afternoon."
8697,"(8697) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh: That Ubayd asked Ali about the prayer. The middle one? He mentioned something similar to this hadith on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 2931, Abu Dawud 412)"
8698,"(8698) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, he said: The middle prayer. Asr prayer"
8699,"(8699) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Umair bin Sa’id, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas He says: {Guard the prayers and the middle prayer} the afternoon prayer."
8700,"(8700) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ali, who said: He is the one who neglected. In it is Ibn Dawud and he is the era."
8701,"(8701) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The middle prayer that he neglected. Sulaiman Asr prayer."
8702,"(8702) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Shurayh was asked about the middle prayer, and he said: Memorize it. You may correct her."
8703,"(8703) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Abiyya, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khuthaym: He was asked about the middle prayer, and he said: This is one of them, so take care of it."
8704,"(8704) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: This is the afternoon."
8705,"(8705) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, that he used to say : {Guard the prayers and the middle prayer} the afternoon prayer.
He said: Ataa was of the opinion that the middle prayer is the lunch prayer."
8706,"(8706) Shababah told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, he said: Hayyan al-Azdi told us, he said: I heard Ibn Umar and he was asked about prayer. Al-Wusti, and it was said to him: Abu Hurairah says: This is the afternoon, and he said: Abu Hurairah increases, Ibn Umar says: This is the morning."
8707,"(8707) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Hafs, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit. On the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The middle prayer is the noon prayer."
8708,"(8708) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Khayyat, who said: I heard Ikrimah say: This is the zihar before it. Two prayers and after that two prayers."
8709,"(8709) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zaid, who said: It is the morning."
8710,"(8710) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: The middle prayer is the afternoon prayer."
8711,"(8711) Shababah told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: “Guard the prayers and the middle prayer” In the morning"
8712,"(8712) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The middle prayer is the afternoon prayer. (Tirmidhi 182. Ahmad 5/12)"
8713,"(8713) Affan narrated to us, he said: Wahb narrated to us, he said: Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qalaab, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Abu Ibn Ka'b said: The middle prayer is the afternoon prayer."
8714,"(8714) Saal bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The middle prayer Asr prayer"
8715,"(8715) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Salat The middle afternoon prayer."
8716,"(8716) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Murā, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: This is the afternoon prayer. (Muslim 2061, Ahmad 1/392)"
8717,"(8717) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qurayh, he said: Abu Raja’ told us, he said: I prayed with Ibn Abbas in the morning prayer in the Basra Mosque. He said: This is the middle prayer."
8718,"(8718) Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: Al-Wasti Fajr prayer"
8719,"(8719) I heard Waki` saying: Sufyan said about a man when the sun had passed the zenith while he was in the city, then he went out on a journey: How? He prays. He said: If it is during the time of noon, he should pray two rak’ahs.
 Hassan bin Salih said: When the sun passed his zenith here, he prayed four times while traveling.
 He said: Sufyan said about a traveler who entered with a resident and prayed a rak’ah prayer with him, then he saw something and spoke, so the imam prayed and said: He will repeat the prayer. The traveler prays two rak'ahs, then returns to the origin he was on.
 Al-Hasan bin Salih said: He prays four times because he has made it obligatory for himself."
8720,"(8720) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan say about a man who entered with the imam on the day of Friday prayer, and he felt anxious, so he went and performed ablution. Then he came and the imam had prayed, but the man did not speak. Sufyan said: The imam’s prayer should be performed in two rak’ahs.
 Al-Hasan bin Salih said: He prays four rak’ahs, unless he prays two rak’ahs with him."
8721,"(8721) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ka’b bin Ajra, he said: We said: O Messenger of God, we have learned how to send peace upon you, so how to send prayers upon you? He said: Say, O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Abraham and the family of Abraham. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious, and bless the Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, just as You blessed Abraham and the family of Abraham. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. (Bukhari 6357, Muslim 66)"
8722,"(8722) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Ka’b Ibn Ajra, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly. (Ahmad 4/244)"
8723,"(8723) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jafar, on the authority of Zayd bin Al-Hadi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Khabbab, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: We said: O Messenger of God, this, peace be upon you, we have known him, so how is the prayer? He said: Say: O God, bless Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, as You bestowed blessings upon Abraham, and bless Muhammad as You bestowed blessings upon his family. Abraham (Bukhari 6358 and Ibn Majah 903)"
8724,"(8724) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mujma’ ibn Yahya, on the authority of Uthman ibn Mawhib, on the authority of Musa ibn Talha, on the authority of His father, he said: We said: O Messenger of God, we have learned that peace be upon you, so how is the prayer? He said: Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Abraham and the family of Abraham. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious, and Blessed. Upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, just as You blessed Abraham and the family of Abraham. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. (Nasa’i 1213. Ahmad 1/162)"
8725,"(8725) Ahmad bin Abdullah told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zaid, on the authority of Uqba bin Amr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came A man greeted him until he sat in front of him and said: O Messenger of God, as for peace be upon you, we have taught him.
 As for prayer, tell us how we may pray for you? He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was silent so much that we wished that the man who asked him had not asked him, then he said: So If you prayed for me, say: O God, bless Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet, and the family of Muhammad, as You prayed for Abraham and the family of Abraham. And bless Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet, and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham and the family of Abraham. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. (Muslim 650, Abu Dawud 973)"
8726,"(8726) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus, Mansour, and Awf told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan: They said, O Messenger of God, you have taught us peace. Upon you, how can we pray for you? He said: Say, O God, bestow Your prayers and blessings upon the family of Muhammad as You made them upon the family of Abraham. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious."
8727,"(۸۷۲۷) حَدَّثَنَا ہُشَیْمٌ ، أَخْبَرَنَا مُغِیرَۃُ ، عَنْ إبْرَاہِیمَ : أَنَّہُ کَانَ إذَا سَلَّمَ أَقْبَلَ عَلَیْنَا بِوَجْہِہِ وَہُوَ Allah says: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partners."
8728,"(8728) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Asim al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: Pray with us. Ali Al-Asr, and when he greeted us, he turned to face us."
8729,"(8729) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Umair bin Sa`id, who said: I heard Abu Musa reciting in congregation {Glorify the Name Your Lord is the Most High. He said: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High."
8730,"(8730) Abdah bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Umair bin Sa’id, who said: I prayed in congregation with Abu Musa. So he recited {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and said: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, while he was in prayer."
8731,"(8731) Abdă and Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Abd Khair: that Ali recited {Glorify the name of your Lord The Most High} and he said: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High. His servant said: While he was in prayer."
8732,"(8732) Abdă told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr reciting {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High} and he said: Glory be to my Lord. The Most High, and He is in prayer."
8733,"(8733) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr reciting {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High} and he said: Glory be to my Lord. The highest"
8734,"(8734) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: that he recited: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} And he said: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High."
8735,"(8735) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Najih, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, the same thing."
8736,"(8736) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid ibn al-Hasan, he said: Urwah ibn Al-Mughirah: When the people led the verse here and he recited {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, he said: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High."
8737,"(8737) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Asbagh bin Zaid, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr: When he recited: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, he would say: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High."
8738,"(8738) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Omar, that whenever he recited: {Glorify the name of your Lord The Most High}, he said, Glory be to my Lord, the Most High."
8739,"(8739) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Muhammad bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, he said: If There is an odd number for you and the imam has an intercession, so do not perform the tashahhud."
8740,"(8740) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: You are witnessing"
8741,"(8741) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who performs a rak’ah with the imam. He said: He recites the tashahhud."
8742,"(8742) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Muslim, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ata’: Concerning a man who catches up with the imam An odd number of prayers. He said: He does not recite the tashahhud.
 Amr bin Dinar said: I see that."
8743,"(8743) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Malik Ibn Anas, who said: I asked Nafi’ and Ibn Shihab about a man who performs a rak’ah first. So he sits with the imam? They said: He recites the Shahada."
8744,"(8744) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever eats of these vile herbs should not approach our mosque, or any other mosque."
8745,"(8745) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever eats this herb should not approach the mosque until its scent has passed away, meaning Garlic (Bukhari 4215. Muslim 69)"
8746,"(8746) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Atiyya, on the authority of Abul-Rabab, on the authority of Maqil bin Saar, he said: I heard him say: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Whoever eats from this tree should not make our prayer offering. It means garlic. (Bukhari 264. Ahmad 5/26)"
8747,"(8747) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal Al-Adawi, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba, who said: I ate garlic, then I came to the prayer place of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and found it. He preceded me in my prayer, and when I stood up to finish it, he smelled the smell of garlic, and said: Whoever eats any of these vegetables should not offer them. Our mosque until its smell goes away, and he said it will change. So when I finished the prayer, I went to it and said: O Messenger of God, I have Excuse me. He gave me your hand. He said: I found him at ease, by God. So he gave me his hand and I put it into my sleeve to my chest. He found him blindfolded and said: You have an excuse. (Abu Dawud 3822. Ibn Hibban 2095)"
8748,"(8748) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Umair bin Qumim al-Taghlabi, on the authority of Sharik bin Hanbal Al-Absi said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever eats of these vile vegetables, let him not. They bring it near our mosque, meaning garlic."
8749,"(8749) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja’d al-Ghatfani, on the authority of Maadan bin Abi Talha Al-Amari: Omar bin Al-Khattab stood up as a Friday sermon as a sermon, or he gave a sermon to us on the day of the Friday prayer, and he said: O people, you are eating two trees that I do not see as anything but evil: this garlic and this onion. I used to see A man at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a scent coming from him, and he was taken by the hand until he was taken out to Al-Baqi`, whoever eats them must surely eat them while cooking them. (Muslim 3971, Ahmad 1/27)"
8750,"(8750) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazeed, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Ayyub, she said: I made The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had some legumes in it, but he did not eat from it and said: I hate to harm him. Your friend (Tirmidhi 1810 and Ahmad 433)"
8751,"(8751) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: Search for Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten days of the month of Ramadan. (Bukhari 2020. Tirmidhi 792)"
8752,"(8752) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights of the month of Ramadan. For the remaining nine, or for seven, or for five, or for three, or for the last night. (Tirmidhi 794. Ahmad 5/36)"
8753,"(8753) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Search for Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights of the month of Ramadan. (Muslim 2060 Abu Daw9 1380)"
8754,"(8754) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Jabalah, and Muharib, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Look forward to Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights of the month of Ramadan. (Muslim 814. Ahmad 2/81)"
8755,"(8755) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Marthad bin Abi Marthad, on the authority of his father, he said: I was with Abu Dharr at the middle Jamarat, and I asked him about Laylat al-Qadr? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to ask people about it. I said: O Messenger of God, the Night of Decree was You will be in the covenant of the prophets, so when they depart you will be exalted? He said: No, but it will remain until the Day of Resurrection. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, inform us about it. He said: If only he had been given permission. I would have told you about it, but seek it out in one of the seventy, and then do not ask me about it after my place or your place. This, then he began a hadith, and when he relaxed I said: O Messenger of God, I swore to you that you would not narrate it to me. Abu Dharr said: So he became angry with me as he had never been angry with me before or after it. (Nasa’i 3427. Ibn Khuzaymah 2170)"
8756,"(8756) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ya’four, on the authority of Abu Al-Salt, on the authority of Abu Aqrab Al-Asadi, he said: We brought Ibn Masoud was in his house, and we found him above the house, and we heard him say before he came down: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth, so we said to him: We heard you say before you descended: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth, and he said: Laylat al-Qadr is on the seventh of the other half, and that is because the sun On that day, it will appear white and without rays, so I looked at the sun and saw it as it was described, so I said “Allahu Akbar.” (Ahmad 1/406; Tayalisi 394)"
8757,"(8757) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I came while I was sleeping during Ramadan. It was said to me: Indeed, the night is the Night of Destiny. He said: I got up while I was sleepy and clung to some of the curtains of the carpet of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying, and I looked during the night and behold... The twenty-third night. He said: Ibn Abbas said: Satan rises with the sun every night except Laylat al-Qadr. That is because it will appear on that day white and without a ray. (Ahmad 1/2551 Tabarani 11777)"
8758,"(8758) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Qanan bin Abdullah Al-Nahmi, who said: I asked Zurra about Laylat Al-Qadr? He said: Omar, Hudhafi and some of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had no doubt that it was the seventh night. And twenty, three remain. He said: Zurr said: So continue it."
8759,"(8759) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Zirr, who said: I heard Ubayy bin Ka’b saying: “Layla.” Al-Qadr is the twenty-seventh night."
8760,"(8760) Abdul-Ala and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah Al-Yazani, on the authority of Al-Sanabihi, he said: I asked Bilal about Laylat Al-Qadr, he said: Laylat Al-Qadr is three. And twenty."
8761,"(8761) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Omar, he said: You have known The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said regarding Laylat al-Qadr: Seek it in the last ten nights at intervals. (Ahmad 1/43, Abu Ali 165)"
8762,"(8762) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Search for the night. The fate is seven to remain, move it to nine to remain, move it to eleven to remain on the morning of a full moon, for the sun is rising Every day between the horns of Satan, except the morning of full moon, then it appears white and has no ray."
8763,"(8763) Amr bin Talha narrated to us, on the authority of Asbat bin Nasr, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights of Ramadan. (Tabarani 1941)"
8764,"(8764) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubaira, on the authority of Ali, who said: He was the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when the last ten nights begin, he wakes up his family and raises his apron. It was said to Abu Bakr: What is the height of the apron? He said: Women’s isolation. (Tirmidhi 7951, Ahmad 1/98)"
8765,"(8765) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Layla The decree in each month of Ramadan."
8766,"(8766) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra, on the authority of Ali; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up his family during the last ten nights of Ramadan. (Tirmidhi 795, Abu Ali 372)"
8767,"(8767) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Whoever performs the prayer for the year He overtook her, he said: And Ubayy said: Abdullah knew that it was in the month of Ramadan, on the twenty-seventh night. (Muslim 220. Abu Dawud 1373)"
8768,"(8768) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khaled narrated to us, saying: I heard Zurr ibn Hubaysh al-Asadi saying: I heard Ubayy He says: It is the night of the twenty-seventh."
8769,"(8769) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik Al-Amiri, who said: I heard Zurr bin Hubaysh He says: When it is the night of the twenty-seventh, then take a bath, and whoever of you is able to delay breaking the fast until dawn, let him do so. And let him break his fast with milk."
8770,"(8770) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Laylat al-Qadr is a night of turbidity, its sun rises but it has no rays."
8771,"(8771) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Shaybah bin Qarith narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Bakr bin Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham says: Laylat al-Qadr is the seventeenth night, the night of Friday."
8772,"(8772) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel and his father narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hujayr al-Taghlabi, on the authority of Al-Aswad. On the authority of Abdullah, he said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr on the night of the seventeenth, for it is the morning of Badr, the Day of Criterion. The day the two groups met."
8773,"(8773) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’a bin Kulthum, who said: I heard Al-Hasan say: This is in all of Ramadan."
8774,"(8774) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Ubad ibn al-Samit, who said: The Messenger of God came out against us. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he wanted to inform them of the Night of Destiny, so two men approached him, and he said: I went out while I I want to inform you of the Night of Decree, and so-and-so and so-and-so approached you, and perhaps that would be good. Seek them in The ninth, seventh, and fifth. (Bukhari 49. Ahmad 5/313)"
8775,"(8775) Shababah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Khubayb, on the authority of Abdullah bin Unais, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace; He was asked about Laylat al-Qadr? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Search for it that night, and that night will be three nights. And twenty. (Abu Dawud 1374. Ahmad 3/495)"
8776,"(8776) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his maternal uncle Al-Faltan bin Asim, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Indeed, I saw Laylat al-Qadr and I forgot about it, so seek it in the last ten nights for a period of time. (Tabarani) 859)"
8777,"(8777) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, who said: I heard Ubayy ibn Ka’b say: The twenty-seventh night, the night about which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed us that the sun It appears white and sparkling. (Muslim 1791, Abu Dawud 1373)"
8778,"(8778) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Sabit, who said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he wakes up his family during the last ten days of Ramadan, and raises his hands during them."
8779,"(8779) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Zaid, on the authority of Aisha; She used to wake up her family on the twenty-third night."
8780,"(8780) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Yazeed; Ibn Abbas used to sprinkle water on his family for the twenty-third night."
8781,"(8781) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He used to wake up his family in The last ten days."
8782,"(8782) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, who said: Abu Bakra used to pray. In Ramadan, like your prayers in the rest of the year, so when the last ten days come, strive hard."
8783,"(8783) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, On the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to strive diligently during the ten days, not He strives hard in other things. (Muslim 8. Tirmidhi 796)"
8784,"(8784) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; {Indeed, We sent it down in the Night of Decree}, he said: the Night of Judgement, {and what makes you know what the Night of Destiny is}, he said: the Night of Judgement. The ruling"
8785,"(8785) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, he said: Her day is like her night, and her night is like Like a word"
8786,"(8786) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Whoever prays the Maghrib and Isha’ prayers in... All together for Laylat al-Qadr, he has taken his share of it."
8787,"(8787) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, he said: Suleiman, the client of Al-Hasan, came to us. Bin Ali in the time of Al-Hajjaj, so he told us on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came one day and people were looking at him, so we said: O Messenger of God, we So that we may see good news in your face. He said: The king came to me and said: O Muhammad, your Lord says: Is it not pleasing to you that he does not pray? Is there anyone from your nation upon you except that I send blessings upon him ten times, and no one greets you except that I greet him ten times? He said: Yes. (Ahmad 4/29, Darmi 2773)"
8788,"(8788) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever prays upon me, the angels will continue to pray upon him as long as He sends blessings upon me, so let the servant do this a little, or let him do it a lot. (Ahmad 3/446, Tayalisi 1142)"
8789,"(8789) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath al-San’ani, on the authority of Aws Ibn Aws said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One of the best days of yours is Friday, on which Adam was created. And in it is the blowing, and in it is the thunderbolt, so pray a lot for me in it, for your prayers will be presented to me, so a man said: Messenger of God, how will our blessings be presented to you when you have died? He means, “Perish,” and he said: “God has forbidden the earth from consuming the bodies of the prophets.”"
8790,"(8790) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of the common people, he said: A man from Banu Asad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that he said: Who May God’s blessings and peace be upon the Prophet, ten good deeds were recorded for him, ten bad deeds were removed from him, and ten degrees were raised for him."
8791,"(8791) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Yazid al-Raqqashi; That an angel was entrusted with the one who prayed upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to inform the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that So-and-so from your nation prayed for you."
8792,"(8792) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Hurr told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Increase your blessings on Friday, for it has been presented to me."
8793,"(8793) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Hurr told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is sufficient for him to be stingy that I should be mentioned in his presence, and then he does not pray for me."
8794,"(8794) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who May God’s blessings be upon him, may God’s prayers be upon him ten times."
8795,"(8795) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Amr, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever prays one blessing upon me, may God’s prayers be upon him ten times, and ten times will be omitted from him. Bad deeds. (Bukhari 643. Ahmad 3/261)"
8796,"(8796) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ka’b, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Pray for me, for praying for me is zakat for you. (Tirmidhi 3612 and Ahmad 2/365)"
8797,"(8797) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Indeed, God has angels who travel on earth, conveying peace to my nation. (Ahmad 1/387, Darmi 2774)"
8798,"(8798) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Tufayl bin Ubayy, on the authority of his father, He said: A man said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: What do you think if I make all of your prayers a prayer upon you? He said: Then God will suffice you with whatever concerns you about the affairs of this world and the hereafter. (Tirmidhi 2457. Ahmad 5/136)"
8799,"(8799) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Ubaidah narrated to me, on the authority of Qais ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa`sa’. On the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Abdul Rahman bin Awf, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said : I prostrated in gratitude to my Lord for what He has bestowed upon me among my nation. Whoever sends a blessing upon me, ten good deeds are recorded for him, and ten are erased from him. Bad deeds."
8800,"(8800) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who forgets to recite the Tashahhud until he comes out of his prayer, and he said: If he left it, then his prayer is complete, and if not He came out of it and recited the tashahhud. He said: It is as if the exit was for him to speak, or to enter into another prayer, or to perform the guardianship. The back of the Qibla"
8801,"(8801) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who forgot to recite the Tashahhud in his prayer, so he said: There is nothing wrong with him, his prayer is permissible."
8802,"(8802) Shababă told us, on the authority of Shu`bā, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who forgets to recite the tash-hud?"
8803,"(8803) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Shubayl, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaddad; Ibn Umar did not sit in the two rak’ahs, so he recited the tashahid twice at the end of his prayer."
8804,"(8804) Ali bin Al-Ja’d narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja’far Al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ghalib, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, he said : If he sits for as long as he has recited the tashahhud, then stops, his prayer has been completed, because not everyone is good at reciting the tashahhud."
8805,"(8805) Wakī’, or someone else, narrated to us on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Muslim Abul-Nadr, on the authority of Ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: He said: Omar: There is no prayer except with the Tashahhud."
8806,"(8806) Ja’far bin Burqan told us, on the authority of Uqba bin Nafi’, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: There is no prayer that does not fulfill it. Recitation, sitting in the two rak’ahs, reciting the tashahhud and salutations. If you do not do that, then you should prostrate two prostrations after the salutations. While you were sitting"
8807,"(8807) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Shuabi narrated to us, on the authority of Muslim Abul Nadr, who said: I heard Hamla bin Abd The Most Gracious says: Omar said: There is no prayer except with the Tashahhud."
8808,"(8808) Hushaym told us, he said: Othman bin Hakim told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I do not know. Prayers should be directed from one to another, except for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
8809,"(8809) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qays, on the authority of Nabih, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. I seek help from you in a debt that my father owed. He said: Go away, I will come to you. So he came to us, and I said to the woman: Do not speak to the Messenger of God, nor do you harm him. When he left, the woman said: O Messenger of God, bless me and my wife. So he said, bless me. May God bless him and grant him peace: May God’s blessings and peace be upon you and your wife. She said: O Messenger of God, do you come to us and do not pray for us? (Ahmad 3/303. Darmi 45)"
8810,"(8810) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace because of my father’s truth, so he accepted it and said: O God, bless my father’s most faithful family. (Bukhari 1497, Muslim 176)"
8811,"(8811) Abdă bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man whose garment is loosened while he is praying, he said: He does not loosen it, nor loosen it, but rather he steps it in. And He raises it."
8812,"(8812) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Muhammad bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: If you want to cover yourself with a loincloth and a cloak while you are praying, then loosen your cloak and wear your cloak. He said: So I mentioned it to Tawus, and he said: It is better, or that is better."
8813,"(8813) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Subaih, on the authority of Abi Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; He disliked for a man to do anything during prayer, even the button of his shirt. He said: And Abraham did not see any harm in lifting it up if his garment was relaxed during prayer."
8814,"(8814) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Salam bin Shaddad Abu Talut al-Jariri narrated to us, on the authority of Ghazwan bin Jarir al-Dhabi, On the authority of his father, he said: When Ali stood for prayer, he would place his right hand on his wrist, and he would not remain like that until he bowed. The same as when he bowed, unless he repaired his garment or rubbed his body."
8815,"(8815) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated to wear his scarf, or to wear clothes while he was praying."
8816,"(8816) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: I recited to Abdullah, and he said: Recite. May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, for indeed the Qur’an is beautified."
8817,"(8817) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; (And recite the Qur’an in a recitation), He said: We have made it clear."
8818,"(8818) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid; (And he recited the Qur’an in a recitation), He said: one part after the other."
8819,"(8819) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: A man from the people of Bajil came to him, and it was said to him: Ibn Sinan went to Ibn Masoud and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, how do you read this letter? Will you find it? A thousand? {from unsullied water}, or {from unsullied water}? He said: Then Abdullah said to him: Did you count the entire Qur’an other than this? He said: So he said to him: Indeed, I recite Al-Mufassal in one rak’ah. He said: This is like this poetry. There are people who recite the Qur’an but it does not go beyond Their throats, but if the Qur’an falls into the heart, it is deeply beneficial. Indeed, the best prayer is bowing and prostration. He said: And Abdullah said: Indeed. I would know the parallels by which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite (Bukhari 7750, Muslim 276)"
8820,"(8820) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim al-Azdi narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, he said: Anas was asked about the reciters of the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: He used to extend his voice with it. (Bukhari 5045. Ahmad 3/119)"
8821,"(8821) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recites: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds. It means, letter by letter. (Tirmidhi 2927. Abu Dawud 3997)"
8822,"(8822) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: Whenever Muhammad recited, he would continue with his recitation."
8823,"(8823) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, who said: He was a generous and generous person who recited this Qur’an."
8824,"(8824) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Mawhib narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi. He says: Because I recite: {When the earth shakes}, {By the one who knocks} for the night I will restore them, and contemplate on them what is dearer to me than to spend the night. This is the Qur’an."
8825,"(8825) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Issa al-Hannat narrated to us, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, he said: Abdullah said: Do not study the Qur’an like this. Poetry, and do not scatter it as a prose, stop at its wonders, and move hearts with it."
8826,"(8826) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Nafi’ bin Omar Al-Jumahi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, on the authority of some of the Prophet’s wives. May God bless him and grant him peace; She was asked about the Prophet’s recitation, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: You cannot do it, so it was said to her: Tell us about it, so she recited a Qur’an with which she was sent."
8827,"(8827) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ubaid al-Mukhtab, he said: Mujahid was asked about two men who recited One of them recited Al-Baqarah, and the other recited Al-Baqarah and the family of Imran, so their bowing, prostration, and sitting were the same, which is the same. Better? He said: The one who recited Al-Baqarah, then Mujahid recited: {And a Qur’an which We have separated so that you may recite it to the people over a period of time, and We have sent it down in a revelation}"
8828,"(8828) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Bayan narrated to us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir, he said: Hudhayfah said: Indeed, who People consider him to be a hypocrite who does not leave out a waw or an alif, and he devours it with his tongue just as cows devour empty words with their tongue. He does not go beyond His collarbone"
8829,"(8829) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja, on the authority of al-Bara’ Ibn Aazib said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Beautify the Qur’an with your voices. (Abu Dawud 1463. An-Nasa’i 1088)"
8830,"(8830) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Naykah. On the authority of Saad, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He is not among us who does not sing the Qur’an. He is satisfied with it. (Abu Dawud 14651. Ahmad 1/179)"
8831,"(8831) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Hassan Al-Makhzoumi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulkiah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Nahik, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who does not sing is not among us. By the Qur’an. That is, he is satisfied with it."
8832,"(8832) Waki’ told us, he said: Abdullah bin Sa’id bin Abi Hind told us, he said: I heard Abu Salma bin Abdul Rahman He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has not given permission to anything like His permission to a prophet who sings of the Qur’an. He recites aloud. (Abdul Razzaq 4169)"
8833,"(8833) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, according to the hadith of Waki’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed. (Bukhari 5023, Muslim 545)"
8834,"(8834) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: The Messenger of God was asked May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Which people are the best readers? He said: When you hear him recite, you will see that he fears God. (Bazzar 2336, Abdul Razzaq 4185)"
8835,"(8835) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, who said: I prayed behind Abraham, but I did not hear him extend, nor return, nor improve. His voice"
8836,"(8836) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: My father told me, he said: They used to hide the tash-hud, but they did not They speak out loudly about it."
8837,"(8837) Mulazim bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of his father Yahya bin Abu Kathir said: Whoever recites the Tashahhud out loud is like one who recites the recitation out loud in a different place."
8838,"(8838) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who prayed two rak'ahs of Maghrib prayer while traveling until he returned. He said: He repeats every prayer he prayed."
8839,"(8839) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alwan ibn Abi Malik, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The steps of prostration Two rak'ahs after sunset, {and the direction of the stars} two rak'ahs before the dawn prayer."
8840,"(8840) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
8841,"(8841) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali He said: {The after-parts of prostration} are two rak'ahs after sunset."
8842,"(8842) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, who said: I heard Al-Hasan say: {the end of the stars} the two rak’ahs before Fajr, {and the afterlife of prostration} the two rak'ahs after sunset."
8843,"(8843) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, who said: I heard Zazan say, similarly."
8844,"(8844) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Uthman al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’a, on the authority of Ali, the same."
8845,"(8845) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: {the steps of prostration} are two rak’ahs after Maghrib, {and the end of the stars} two rak'ahs before dawn."
8846,"(8846) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, he said: {the direction of the stars} Two rak'ahs before dawn, {and after prostration} two rak'ahs after sunset."
8847,"(8847) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Aws bin Khalid, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: “Aspects of the stars” are two rak’ahs before dawn, and “the backs of prostration” are two rak’ahs after sunset."
8848,"(8848) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He was the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he prays his prayer at night while I am at a distance between him and the tribe, so if he wants to He prayed the Witr. He woke me up and I performed the Witr. (Muslim 266)"
8849,"(8849) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzali al-Jumahi, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr led us in prayer, so it passed. There was a woman before us after we had prayed one or two rak'ahs, but he did not care about her."
8850,"(8850) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Talha bin Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba, on the authority of Aisha She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying at night, and I was beside him while I was menstruating, and he was wearing a cloak for me. And some of it is upon him. (Muslim 274. Ahmad 6/67)"
8851,"(8851) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Fara`i, he said: I asked Sa`id bin Jubayr about A woman passes in front of a man while he is praying? He said: Nothing interrupts the prayer."
8852,"(8852) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He mentioned To Him, the woman, the donkey, and the dog interrupt the prayer. Ibn Abbas said: (To Him ascend good words and righteous deeds. He raises him) Nothing interrupts the prayer, but it is disliked."
8853,"(8853) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The imam leads the row, and the rows lead one another."
8854,"(8854) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: I was informed on the authority of Masruq that he said: People are imams of one another in Rows"
8855,"(8855) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: When he performs rak’ahs there is no prostration between them, so"
8856,"(8856) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir; Concerning a man who prayed Maghrib four times, he said: He will repeat the prayer."
8857,"(8857) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who prayed Maghrib four times, he said: He prostrates the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
8858,"(8858) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, who said: A man asked Al-Hassan about a man who only does good. {Say: Allah is One} Should he lead his people and celebrate them? He said: Yes."
8859,"(8859) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: If a man does not have anything of the Qur’an with him except a surah One, he recited it in his prayer and repeated it."
8860,"(8860) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Mughirah; That Abu An-Nadr asked Al-Hasan, and he said: Do I lead my people, and I only recite: {Say: He is God, One}. Should I repeat it? He said: Yes."
8861,"(8861) Harun told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The roof is like a desert home, if there is no veil."
8862,"(8862) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to like, when they entered Mecca, not to leave until They conclude the Qur’an with it."
8863,"(8863) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Al-Qalama recited the Qur’an one night in Mecca, and he circumambulated. He stayed at home for a week, then he came to the shrine and prayed there, so he recited “Al-Mi’in”, then he circumambulated for a week, then he came to the shrine and prayed there, so he recited. reciting the double prayer, then he circumambulated for seven weeks, then he came to the shrine and prayed there, then he recited the rest of the Qur’an."
8864,"(8864) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They were amazed when they came for Hajj, or They are not to go out until they have recited what they have of the Qur’an."
8865,"(8865) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: He used to like, or would recommend, if He has come to any of these mosques, not to leave until the Qur’an has been read in the Sacred Mosque, or the Mosque of Medina, or Bayt Al-Maqdis Mosque."
8866,"(8866) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: When a Thaqif delegation came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace They encamped in a basement that was at the back of the mosque, and when the time for prayer came, a man from the people said: O Messenger of God, you have attended the prayer. These are a people of infidels, and they are in the mosque. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The land is not impure, or something like that. This (Abu Dawud 17)"
8867,"(8867) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; A Thaqif delegation came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in the mosque, in his dome, and he was told: The Messenger of God, they are polytheists, so he said: The land cannot be impure by anything."
8868,"(8868) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’bā narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Asqalani, that he informed him of the one who saw Ibn Muhairiz shook hands with a Christian in a Damascus mosque."
8869,"(8869) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Al-Haytham, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Mujahid; He saw no harm in the People of the Book sitting in the mosque."
8870,"(8870) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: Do not sit as a judge in a mosque. Both Jews and Christians enter it."
8871,"(8871) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: Not for the polytheists. That they should not enter the mosque except in fear."
8872,"(8872) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Ezza, who said: Al-Sha’bi used to pray. He is sitting, and he sits as you sit in prayer."
8873,"(8873) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, who said regarding the prayer of one who is sitting: He sits in a row. I wish"
8874,"(8874) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, something like Al-Sha’bi’s work, that he used to do it."
8875,"(8875) Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Omar bin Muhammad bin narrated to me. Hatib, he said: A great man from the Persians came to Omar and asked about Omar, and he was told: He is leaving Medina, so he went out to him. He said: Then he met him as he was coming, and the young man turned away and prostrated, or to prostrate. Abdullah was in doubt. He said: Then Omar said: Raise your head. To the One, the Sublime."
8876,"(8876) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of a man called: Muthanna, who said: A priest came to Ali and prostrated himself. Then he forbade him and said: Prostrate to Him."
8877,"(8877) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Mu’adh, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: If I were to command someone to prostrate to anyone else, I would command women to prostrate to their husbands.
(Ahmad 5/227 Tabarani 373)"
8878,"(8878) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Misra; When the non-Arabs prostrated to Salman, he bowed his head and said: I submit to God."
8879,"(8879) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: He said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: If I had ordered anyone to prostrate to anyone else, the women would have been to their husbands. (Abu Dawud 2)"
8880,"(8880) Affan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If I had ordered anyone to prostrate to anyone else, I would have ordered women to prostrate to their husbands. (Ahmad 6/76. An-Nasa’i 9147)"
8881,"(8881) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Qurayh bin Khalid Al-Sadoosi narrated to us, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani; Omar asked permission to come to Abd al-Rahman bin Awf while he was praying in his house, and Omar said to him: Briefly."
8882,"(8882) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: So A man sat next to one of you while he was praying, so let him leave."
8883,"(8883) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Janab Yahya ibn Abi Hayyya al-Kalbi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Juwayriyah. Al-Jarmiyy, he said: We sat behind Ibn Abbas while he was praying behind the Maqam, and he was wearing a piece of velvet for him. He said: So we talked, and when he heard Our voices are gone."
8884,"(8884) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, on the authority of Zaid ibn constant; He was asked about recitation during the noon and afternoon prayers? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray for a long time and move his lips. (Ahmad 5/1864 Tabarani 4886)"
8885,"(8885) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Muammar, he said: We said to Khabab: With anything. Did you know the recitation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at noon and afternoon? He said: Because of the disorder in his beard."
8886,"(8886) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite at noon and afternoon prayers. (Abu Dawud 8050. Ahmad 1/234)"
8887,"(8887) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`d bin Iyad al-Thumali, who said: I did not pray. A prayer unless you recite it."
8888,"(8888) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Because he hated to recite the Qur’an."
8889,"(8889) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I came to Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla. With arrogance, he said: Is it possible that I might be given a copy of the Qur’an with it?"
8890,"(8890) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: There is no harm in unraveling the Qur’an."
8891,"(8891) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Shuaib bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Ubayy, who said: If you Your Qur’anic copies and the adornment of your mosques, so the end will be upon you."
8892,"(8892) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Abu Umamah; He disliked for the Qur’an to be unraveled."
8893,"(8893) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said about a drunk person leading the people in prayer. He said: When he completes the bowing with them And prostration is sufficient for him and for them. Muhammad said: They will celebrate Eid together, including the Imam."
8894,"(8894) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Muslim ibn Jundub, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Barsa’ah. He said: Khubayb was brought and sold in Mecca, so they took him out of the sanctuary to kill him, and he said: Let me pray two rak’ahs. So they left him, and he prayed two rak'ahs, then he said: Had you not thought that I was anxious, I would have done more."
8895,"(8895) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: When he was taken with a stone to Mu’awiyah, he said: Peace be upon you. Commander of the Faithful, he said: And the Commander of the Faithful am I? He said: Yes. He said: I will kill you. He said: Then he ordered him to be killed. He said: Let me pray two rak’ahs. So he prayed two rak’ahs. He passed through them and said: You do not see that I made them weak out of fear, but I did not like to be too long for you. Then he was killed."
8896,"(8896) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The twilight is the fire."
8897,"(8897) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to us: Pray the Maghrib prayer. When the fasting person broke his fast, then it was mentioned to me: There are people who hasten the evening prayer before the whiteness of the horizon disappears from the west. You will pray until the white of the horizon disappears from the west, and the darkness of the night covers you, and you do not hasten after the white of the horizon has disappeared from Morocco, for it is better and more correct, and know that among its completeness and correctness is its time, which I have mentioned to you in this book of mine. Because the whiteness of the horizon disappears, it is a remnant of the rest of the day."
8898,"(8898) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khathim, on the authority of Ibn Labiba, he said: He said to Abu Hurairah: Pray the Isha’ prayer when twilight has gone, and the night’s darkness has passed between you and a third of the night, and do not hasten after it has gone. A whiter horizon is better."
8899,"(8899) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Hanzali, he said: Tawoos was praying the evening prayer before he disappeared. Whiteness"
8900,"(8900) Yunus bin Muhammad bin Sharik told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The twilight is what remains of the day."
8901,"(8901) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad; Abdullah bin Rabi’ah used to lead his companions in voluntary prayers other than Ramadan."
8902,"(8902) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Rabi’, on the authority of Itban bin Malik, that He said: O Messenger of God, the floods are preventing me from the mosque of my people, so I would like you to come and pray in a place I will take my house as a mosque. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: We will do so. When the morning came, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Tomorrow he greeted Abu Bakr and he followed him. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered, he said: Where do you want? So I pointed to him towards one side of the house, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, and we lined up behind him, and he led us in prayer. Two rak'ahs (Bukhari 424, Muslim 455)"
8903,"(8903) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Badr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Musa, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The two and above are combined. (Ibn Majah 972 and Abu Ali 7188)"
8904,"(8904) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham al-Dastawwi told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When he prayed A man is with another man, so they are together. For them, the double is twenty-five degrees."
8905,"(8905) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The three are collective."
8906,"(8906) Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you knit any of Your body while you are bowing, so do not raise your head until you return your hand to its place."
8907,"(8907) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who said: Haha in prayer, he said: Eid."
8908,"(8908) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated to recite in prayer."
8909,"(8909) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He disliked exhaling during prayer. He said: It is likened to speech."
8910,"(8910) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by May God’s peace and blessings be upon Bilal while he was reciting from this surah, and from this surah, and he said: I passed by you, Bilal. And you were reciting from this surah, and from this surah, and he said: By my father, O Messenger of God, I wanted to mix The good for the good, he said: Read the surah in the same way. (Abu Dawud 1324; Abd al-Razzaq 4210)"
8911,"(8911) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Ammar used to mix some of this surah with some of this surah, so it was said: Why? He said: Do you see me mixing in it something that is not part of it?"
8912,"(8912) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muhammad was asked about the one who recites from here, and from Here? He said: To be pious, not to commit a grave sin without realizing it."
8913,"(8913) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Al-Walid bin Juma’ narrated to us, saying: A man I trust narrated to me; The leader of the people in confusion was Khalid ibn al-Walid. He recited from various surahs, then he turned to us when he left and said: We have been distracted by jihad. About learning the Qur’an."
8914,"(8914) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to hate to recite from two surahs until he completed one, then he started on the other."
8915,"(8915) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: They used to say about the one who prays without I read it in a severe way, I hate to say it."
8916,"(8916) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If neither the imam nor those behind him recite, they repeat the prayer. All of them"
8917,"(8917) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If I prayed behind a man who I did not know was reciting, I would repeat. Your prayers"
8918,"(8918) Azhar al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad used to hate to say: We missed the prayer, and he would say: Why? I join you with the children of so-and-so."
8919,"(8919) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Laith, who said: Tawoos used to crouch when he prostrated, and would turn away. His elbows are lower than his thighs when he bows."
8920,"(8920) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Laith, who said: Nafi’ used to keep his elbows away from his thighs."
8921,"(8921) Waki’ told us, he said: Humayd told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Laith, he said: I saw Mujahid bending his elbows. About the width of his thighs, while he was prostrating during prayer, and I saw Ataa doing the same."
8922,"(8922) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, Muhammad bin Ali, Ata’, Tawoos, Al-Qasim, and Mujahid, They said: There is no harm for a man to pray the written prayer and other things, with the tablets on the sleeve, and the parchment with poetry on it. And the likes of it."
8923,"(8923) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no harm in a man praying with tablets behind him. And the newspaper."
8924,"(8924) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He saw no harm in praying, even though he had the dirhams in his possession."
8925,"(8925) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yasir bin Amr; He did not lower himself when he prostrated."
8926,"(8926) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father; Omar wanted not to attack the mosque, so Sufyan bin Abdullah Al-Thaqafi advised him and said: Yes, Amir. The believers, for he is more forgiving of the pitfalls and more accommodating to the assembly. Omar said: Count him."
8927,"(8927) Abd al-Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, who said: My father was in a place that was not clean, and I attended him. So he ordered a carpet to be spread out, then he prayed for it."
8928,"(8928) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, who said: Mujahid saw me clearing a place on our roof. We pray in it, and he said: Do not sprinkle, for sprinkling only increases evil, but look at the place where you want to prostrate. So he blew it."
8929,"(8929) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Ali used to say between the two prostrations: My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, help me, and raise me above me."
8930,"(8930) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He used to say between the two prostrations: O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, help me, and provide for me. (Tirmidhi 284, Ahmad 315)"
8931,"(8931) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Umm Al-Hasan, on the authority of Umm Salama, that She used to say between the two rak'ahs or two prostrations: O God, forgive and have mercy and show the right path."
8932,"(8932) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, who said: My father used to recite a lot of Qur’an between the two prostrations."
8933,"(8933) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ata, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said the salaam between the two prostrations: I ask forgiveness from God, I ask forgiveness from God. (Abu Dawud 870. An-Nasa’i 656)"
8934,"(8934) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is nothing temporary about it."
8935,"(8935) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I asked Ibrahim: Should I recite something between the two prostrations? He said: No."
8936,"(8936) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Abu Muhammad bin Amr bin Harith, on the authority of His grandfather, he heard Abu Hurairah say: If one of you prays in a land of lava, let him set up a stick, and if he does not have a stick with him Let him draw a line on the ground, and whatever passes between his hands will not harm him. Abu al-Qasim said: He means a narration. (Abu Dawud 690; Ibn Majah 943)"
8937,"(8937) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, he said: He wanted A person was about to set up something in the presence of a peacock while he believed it, but he prevented it."
8938,"(8938) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abu Hilal told us, he said: Hamid bin Hilal told us, on the authority of Abu Burda; That Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari came in to see his sister while she was prostrating without bowing, so that did not bother her."
8939,"(8939) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq; He saw a man praying three prostrations in a rak’ah, and he said: God is satisfied with each rak’ah with two prostrations."
8940,"(8940) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There are four that the imam does not dare to pronounce. ; In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, and seek refuge, and Amen, and praise be to God, our Lord."
8941,"(8941) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Five things that the imam hides; Seeking refuge, Glory be to God, and praise be to You, and in the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, and Amen, and to God, our Lord, praise be to You."
8942,"(8942) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They were hiding their seeking refuge."
8943,"(8943) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I heard Omar say: When he opened the prayer Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and blessed be Your name, and exalted is Your glory, and there is no god but You. Al-Aswad said: He hears us."
8944,"(8944) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn and Mughiry told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The imam is hidden in the name of God. The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, and seek refuge, and Amen, and our Lord, praise be to You."
8945,"(8945) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Saad bin Marzban, he said: Abu Wael told us, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to hide in the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, and seeking refuge, and our Lord, praise be to You."
8946,"(8946) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Ja’far al-Ahmar, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Ata’, he said: What happened on the authority of When a person prays, he does something that has its basis in the Qur’an, so it is not just words."
8947,"(8947) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: I saw Abu Qalab wearing a robe and a washed quilt, and he He prays while lying down, with his right hand out."
8948,"(8948) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: It was said to Al-Hasan: They say: It is disliked for a man to pray. And he had taken his hand out from his throat. Al-Hasan said: If God had entrusted His religion to these people, they would have imposed hardship on His servants."
8949,"(8949) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Hayyan ibn Umair, who said: I was with Qais ibn Abbad, and he saw A man was praying, he had taken his hand out from where his throat was, and he said: Go to that man and tell him: He should put his hand where his hand was. So I came to him and said: Qais is saying: Put your hand where the hand of the fettered one was, so he put it down."
8950,"(8950) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Tawus, who said: I saw him praying, holding his cloak under his arm."
8951,"(8951) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Omar said: It does not harm him even if he wears antiques with it. He takes out one of his hands."
8952,"(8952) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you are wearing a shirt and a quilt, then cover yourself with the quilt. If it is clay and a quilt, then use the quilt."
8953,"(8953) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you are wearing a fine shirt and a quilt, So cover yourself with a quilt, and if it is a tight shirt and a quilt, then cover yourself with a quilt."
8954,"(8954) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Abd al-Malik al-Taymi, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The beginning of the row means the imam, If there is only one person with the imam, he should make him stand behind him and make it clear that he should bow, then if someone comes to lead him in prayer, If no one comes and kneels, he should follow the imam and stand on his right, and if he comes and the row is complete, then he should stand up to the imam. Someone came to pray with him, and if no one came, let him join the line, then such and such and such."
8955,"(8955) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he comes and the row has been completed, let him stand in the imam’s shoes."
8956,"(8956) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Ibn Sirin about a woman who is menstruating. A known number of days, and more than that? He said: Women know better about that.
 He said: I asked his leaders, I said: A woman menstruates for the specified days, so does it exceed five days? He said: Do you pray? I said: So four days? He said: You pray. I said: Three days? He said: You pray. I said: For two days? He said: That was during her menstruation, and I saw him saying his opinion."
8957,"(8957) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Al-Zabarqan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Tawus, said: If a woman has more than her menstrual period, then she should perform ablution. Hammad said regarding a woman who exceeds the days of her menstruation. He said: Do not wash, for the woman may have done that."
8958,"(8958) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas, who said: If she saw A yellow woman on days other than her menstruation, he said: If she adds one or two days to the days of her menstruation, If she has been menstruating for six days, she sees blood. She counted eight days from her menstruation, so if she saw it for more than eight days, then she is undergoing menstruation."
8959,"(8959) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I heard Ayyub speaking, on the authority of Abu Qulabab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said : The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said while he was giving good tidings to his companions: A blessed month of Ramadan has come to you. It was assumed You must fast, during which the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained. In it, the Night of Decree is better than a thousand months. Whoever is deprived of its goodness has been deprived. (Muslim 758. Ahmad 2/230)"
8960,"(8960) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Arfaja, who said: I was with Utba bin Farqad and he He was speaking to us about the virtue of Ramadan, then a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon us, and Utbah remained silent as if he were Abu So-and-so, when he sat down, Utbah said to him: O father of so-and-so, tell us what you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Ramadan, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The gates of Paradise are opened and the gates of Paradise are closed. Fire, and the devils will be chained therein, and a herald will call out every night: O seeker of good, come, O seeker of evil. shorter (Ahmad 5/411)"
8961,"(8961) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. ; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to perform Ramadan without any resolve, and he said: When Ramadan begins, the prayers will be opened. The gates of Paradise, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are in chains. (Bukhari 1898, Muslim 523)"
8962,"(8962) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Nadhar bin Ali, on the authority of Nadhar bin Shayban, who said: I asked Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, Then he mentioned on the authority of his father. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever fasts out of faith and seeking reward, will be forgiven for his previous sins. His sin"
8963,"(8963) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of al-Fadl al-Raqqashi, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Anas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This Ramadan has come, the gates of Paradise will be opened and the gates of Paradise will be closed. Hell, and the devils will be chained therein, after the one who catches up with Ramadan and will not be forgiven in it. If he is not forgiven in it, then when? (Tabarani 7623)"
8964,"(8964) Hushaym told us, saying: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali; When Ramadan came, he would deliver a sermon and say: This is the blessed month in which God has enjoined fasting on you, and He did not It is obligatory for you to perform it."
8965,"(8965) Hushaym told us, saying: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq; Omar used to say something like that."
8966,"(8966) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Muslim ibn al-Ala’, on the authority of a man from Quraysh, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: The first thing that will happen to the one who prays and fasts well in Ramadan is to finish it while it is like a day. His mother gave birth to him from sins."
8967,"(8967) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, all his previous sins will be forgiven. (Bukhari 2014, Muslim 175)"
8968,"(8968) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Kathir bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Tamim, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This man of yours is the most unjust of you according to what the Messenger of God swore. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. No month has entered upon the Muslims that is better for them, and no month has entered upon the hypocrites that is worse for them. From him"
8969,"(8969) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his past deeds will be forgiven. (Nasa’i 2502)"
8970,"(8970) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Umays, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Hanafi, on the authority of his brother Taliq Ibn Qays, he said: Abu Dharr said: When you fast, be careful as much as you can. He was free when it was the day of his fast and he entered and did not come out except To pray."
8971,"(8971) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If it is a day of fasting for one of you, let him not be obscene, nor be ignorant. Someone should say: I am a fasting person."
8972,"(8972) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If it is a day of fasting for one of you, let him not be obscene, nor be ignorant. If anyone is ignorant of him, let him say: Indeed. A fasting man. (Bukhari 1904, Muslim 857)"
8973,"(8973) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: Jabir said: If you fast, let your hearing fast. And keep your sight and tongue away from lying and sin, and refrain from harming the servant, and may there be dignity and tranquility upon you on the day of your fast, and do not Make the day of your breaking the fast and the day of your fasting the same."
8974,"(8974) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Abi Al-Mutawakkil; When Abu Hurairah and his companions fasted, they would sit in the mosque."
8975,"(8975) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Omar said: Fasting is not from food and drink alone, but from Lying, falsehood, idle talk, and swearing."
8976,"(8976) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, who said: I heard Maimun say: The easiest way to fast is to abstain from food and drink."
8977,"(8977) Hushaym told us, saying: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, who said: Fasting does not consist of food and drink. But from lies, falsehood and idle talk."
8978,"(8978) Hushaym told us, saying: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq; Omar said something like that."
8979,"(8979) Waki’ and Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari; That a woman used to fast during the covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: She did not fast and be careful. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: She almost did, then she was afraid, so he said: Now."
8980,"(8980) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Two characteristics of those who memorize them are that their fasting is safe; Backbiting and lying"
8981,"(8981) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to say: Lying breaks the fast."
8982,"(8982) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, who said: The fasting person is among his servants. He did not backbite."
8983,"(8983) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi’, on the authority of Yazid ibn Aban, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: He who continues to eat people’s meat does not fast."
8984,"(8984) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hind, he said: Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakheer said: I went to Othman bin Abi Al-Aas and he prayed for me with milk from a fertile woman. I said: I am fasting, so he said: I am fasting. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Fasting is a protection from Hell, just as one of you is a protection against fighting, and fasting is good. Fasting for three days of every month. (Nasa’i 2539. Ahmad 4/21)"
8985,"(8985) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra, who said: Abdullah said: Fasting is a shield from Hell. Like a man's insanity when he carries as much weapon as he can handle."
8986,"(8986) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hariri, and Abu Sa’id, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: God says: Fasting is for Me and I will reward it. Indeed, the fasting person has two joys; When he breaks his fast he rejoices, and when he meets God he rejoices, and by the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the smell of the mouth of a fasting person is sweeter to God than the fragrance of Musk (Muslim 807. Ahmad 3/5)"
8987,"(8987) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Every good deed of the son of Adam is multiplied ten times to seven hundred times. God Almighty said: Except Fasting is for Me and I will reward it. He gives up his food, drink and lust for My sake. The fasting person has two joys; His joy when he breaks his fast, and his joy when he meets his Lord, and the contentment therein is sweeter to God than the scent of musk. Fasting is a paradise. Fasting is paradise. (Muslim 164. Ahmad 2/443)"
8988,"(8988) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Mahdi bin Maimun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yaqoub, on the authority of Raja’ bin Huwah, on the authority of Abu Umamah, said: I said: O Messenger of God, instruct me to do an act by which I will enter Paradise, or something like that, and he said: You must fast, for there is no other like it. He said: Abu Imamah was never seen in his house by smoke during the day unless it descended there. guest (Nasa’i 2530, Ahmad 5/249)"
8989,"(8989) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl ibn Sa`d al-Sa`idi, who said: Heaven has a door. Al-Rayyan is called Al-Rayyan and those who are fasting enter it. He said: When the last of them enter, it is closed. (Tabarani 6. Ibn Hibban 3421)"
8990,"(8990) Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad Al-Sa’idi, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace, likewise. (Bukhari 1896, Muslim 166)"
8991,"(8991) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Bashar bin Abi Saif, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Iyadh bin Ghataif, he said: We entered upon Abu Ubaidah, and he said: Fasting is a sin as long as you do not break it."
8992,"(8992) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: Bashar bin Abi Saif told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Iyad bin Ghataif, who said: We visited Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah during his illness, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Fasting is a sin as long as one does not break it. (Ahmad 1/1961 Bayhaqi 171)"
8993,"(8993) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, he said: We went out as a delegation. To Muawiyah, we passed by a monk who was bringing food, and the people ate, and I did not eat, so he said to me: Why do you not eat? So I said: I am fasting. He said: Should I not reward you for your fast? The tables are set and the first to eat from them are those who are fasting."
8994,"(8994) Zayd bin Harun told us, and Abu Asama said: Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Wasil, my father’s client. Ayna, he said: A foundling narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: We were in the sea and while we were walking We had raised the sail, and we did not see an island or anything, when we heard a caller calling: O people of the ship, stand still, I will inform you. So we stood up to look but did not see anything, so he called for seven people, and when it was the seventh time, I got up and said: Hey, tell us what you want to do. You tell us about it, because you see our situation, and we cannot stand up to you. He said: Shall I not inform you of the decree that God has decreed upon Himself? Whenever a servant thirsts himself for the sake of God on a hot day, he will quench his thirst with God on the Day of Resurrection. Abu Asama added: You did not want to see Abu Musa fasting on a day far away between the two ends, but you saw him."
8995,"(8995) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’dan al-Janni, on the authority of Sa’d Abi Mujahid al-Tai’i, on the authority of Abi Mudalliyah, on the authority of Abi Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The fasting person will not have his supplications rejected. (Ibn Majah 1752. Ahmad 2/445)"
8996,"(8996) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: For every people of good deeds there is a gate from the gates of Paradise from which they will be called. With that action, and for those who fast, there is a chapter called: Al-Rayyan. (Bukhari 1897, Muslim 85)"
8997,"(8997) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; That Abu Talha used to fast frequently during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he would not break his fast after him except those who Pain"
8998,"(8998) Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He would hardly break his fast in the city unless he fell ill."
8999,"(8999) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: He was among those who fasted a lot. Ibn Omar, Aisha, and Saeed bin Al-Musayyab."
9000,"(9000) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; Omar began fasting two years before his death."
9001,"(9001) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Jumhan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: There is a zakat for everything, and the zakat of the body is fasting. (Ibn Majah 1745)"
9002,"(9002) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: It was said to Abdullah: You are fasting less frequently, and he said: I am afraid that He prevented me from reciting the Qur’an, and reciting the Qur’an is more beloved to me than fasting."
9003,"(9003) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhajir, who said: They believed that fasting was the least rewarding type of fasting."
9004,"(9004) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Maymun narrated to us, on the authority of his father; That a man said to Abu Dharr: Fasting, I do not hear you mention it? Abu Dharr said: He is close to you, but he is not there for you."
9005,"(9005) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: One of the least of their deeds was fasting."
9006,"(9006) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: Have suhoor, for there is blessing in suhoor. (Muslim 770. Bukhari 1923)"
9007,"(9007) Waki’ and Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Have suhoor, for there is a blessing in suhoor. (Ahmad 2/477, Abu Ali 6366)"
9008,"(9008) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Qays, the client of Amr bin Al-Aas, on the authority of Amr Ibn Al-Aas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The separation between your fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is complete. Magic (Muslim 771. Ahmad 4/197)"
9009,"(9009) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: Whoever wants to fast should eat the suhoor meal, even if it is with something. (Abu Ali 1926. Ahmad 3/367)"
9010,"(9010) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Have the suhoor meal, even if it is just a little water. (Ibn Hibban 3476 and Abu Ali 3340)"
9011,"(9011) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, who said: She used to hope for the pre-dawn blessing."
9012,"(9012) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, she said: Have suhoor even by drinking some water. For his supplication has been mentioned."
9013,"(9013) Muttalib bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Have suhoor, for there is a blessing in suhoor. (Ahmad 3/32)"
9014,"(9014) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Muwarriq Al-Ijlili, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: Who The morals of the prophets: reporting the suhoor meal."
9015,"(9015) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told me, he said: Yunus bin Saif Al-Ansi told me, On the authority of Al-Harith ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Rum Al-Sama’i, that he heard Irbad ibn Sariya saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called us May the peace and blessings of God be upon him during the month of Ramadan until the pre-dawn meal, and he said: Come to the blessed lunch. (Abu Dawud 2337. Ahmad 4/126)"
9016,"(9016) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer.” (Bukhari 617, Tirmidhi 203)"
9017,"(9017) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiyyah, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Do not prevent any of you from saying Bilal’s call to prayer during his suhoor meal, for he is calling, or giving the call to prayer at night. Then your sleeper will wake up, and your guardian will return. (Bukhari 621, Abu Dawud 2339)"
9018,"(9018) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar (h) and on the authority of al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha; Bilal used to give the call to prayer at night, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Eat and drink until Ibn Umm gives the call to prayer. Muffled (Bukhari 1919. Muslim 768)"
